- Done: the tests pass; `scripts/screenshot /tmp/x.png` shows Earth''s limb across the lower half and the label; `./sly start`, `./sly play`, `./sly eval ''(sim-t (game-sim *game*))''` twice a second apart differ by about 1 s; the window closes with Escape.

### 3. `assets.lisp`, the Blue Marble and its packaging (needs web access: `--web`)
- Fetch `world.200401.3x5400x2700.jpg` (the URL in `docs/design.md` "The places" → "Sources"), check its size (~1.8 MB) and that it decodes to 5400×2700, commit it as `assets/earth/blue-marble-5400.jpg` with `assets/earth/SOURCE.md` (URL, date fetched, licence text of NASA''s media guidelines as quoted in `docs/luv-capabilities.md`, credit "NASA Earth Observatory (Blue Marble Next Generation)", no NASA logo, the file''s SHA-256) and `CREDITS.md` at the root with the credit (`decision 13`). Without web access the worker stops and records it, as `decision 45: Web access for pm workers still denied after decision 28` did.
- `assets.lisp`: `(assets-root &optional (env (uiop:getenv "LUV_IN_SPACE_ASSETS")))`: the variable when set and non-empty, else `(asdf:system-relative-pathname "luv-in-space" "assets/")`; `(asset-path relative)` signalling a clear error when the file is missing; `(load-image-pixels path)`: decode with `sdl3-image`, convert to ABGR8888, copy into a rank-2 `(unsigned-byte 32)` array rows × columns, free the surfaces, a typed copy loop.
