## Sources and decisions
- Specification: `docs/design.md` "Scope" → "Feature list", the row "Map, basic: Earth, the osculating orbit with Ap/Pe and impact markers, zoom to 100 AU" (must, 2); "Views" → Map (focus, range, ×1.2 per notch, ×10 per Page key, 0.15 s easing, opening frame, the 6 px rule, lines, colours, fixed exposure); "Controls" (M, Tab, Page-up / Page-down, right drag, wheel; `decision 29: Control scheme: key map, control modes, gamepad`); colours of "The cockpit" → "Readability" (cyan #40D0FF own ship, red #FF3030, grey #8A8A80 labels, paper white #E8E4D8).
- Files and load order: `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`decision 12: Module layout and package split`): `camera.lisp` (extended), `ribbons.lisp` (new, after `meshes.lisp`, before `post.lisp`), `post.lisp` and `overlay.lisp` (extended), `input.lisp`, `main.lisp`, `capture.lisp` (extended); tests `tests/camera.lisp`, `tests/ribbons.lisp` (new, after `tests/meshes.lisp` or the last rendering test before `tests/post.lisp`), `tests/post.lisp`, `tests/overlay.lisp` (new if part 4 made none), `tests/input.lisp`, `tests/render.lisp` (GPU).
- Rendering: `docs/architecture.md` "Frames" (camera FRD, the camera stored relative to the ship or a body), "Rendering precision" (draw order: ribbons after meshes, depth-tested, no depth write, additive), "Floating-origin pitfalls" (orbit lines in double relative to their body, made eye-relative each frame), "GPU tests"; `decision 4: Depth strategy`, `decision 5: Precision of positions`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`, `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure` (stage 3 overlay, `*exposure-map*`), `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 7: Placeholder labels: dot-matrix overlay quads`.
- luv: `docs/luv-capabilities.md` "Orbit lines and markers" (triangle lists only, the ribbon of run 32 in `docs/luv-capabilities.md`''s gap-probe appendix: one instance per segment, a 6-vertex quad expanded in the vertex shader), "Rendering" (bind groups after each `set-pipeline`, `canvas-frame-resource-cache` for per-frame buffers).
- Orbits: `decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic` (ellipses and hyperbolas alike, apoapsis nil on a hyperbola); crash radius R⊕ + 100 km (`decision 34: How death works`, `bodies.lisp`).
- Input and cameras: `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 82: Outside view camera: angles in a frame, toggles that keep the picture, distance and easing` (drag signs, log easing).
- Recorded for this plan: `decision 83: Map camera: framing on opening, focus, zoom, drag and exposure`, `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility`.
- Tests: `docs/architecture.md` "Testing" → "Rules for tests" (`scripts/test` under ~15 s), "GPU tests" (image checks from a set state, never pixel-exact).

## Rules for every piece
- Rendering files read the simulation state and never change it; the map camera and view live in the `game` (`map-view` slot, `:initform`), not in the `sim`: checkpoints, restarts and determinism don''t see them (`decision 83`).
- Precision (`decision 5`): orbit vertices, marker points and the eye are double; only (point − eye) in double becomes single; no single-float cache of anything that moves.
- Pure parts (map camera, framing, zoom, ribbon points and splitting, marker positions, visibility, projected sizes, label text) are functions of the render state and the camera, tested without a canvas; per-frame paths cons nothing (preallocated buffers, checked with a 1,000-frame loop as part 4''s tests do).
- Live redefinition ("Dev loop"): tunables are `defparameter`s citing their decision; the ribbon pipeline is a live shader pipeline with its own role; per-frame instance data through `canvas-frame-resource-cache`.
- Each piece adds its files to `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems), passes `scripts/test` and `scripts/screenshot`, and keeps `AGENTS.md` ("Layout") and `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" true. A luv gap met goes to `docs/luv-capabilities.md` and `docs/luv-wishlist.md`.

## Pieces, in the order they run

### 1. The map camera and view: M, Tab, wheel, Page keys, drag, Home, exposure
- `camera.lisp` (`decision 83`): `map-view` struct: focus `:earth` or `:ship`, basis e1, e2, n (double vec3s), azimuth, elevation, distance, target distance; `(map-view-open! view render-state)`: basis from the render state (n = unit r × v, e1 = unit r, e2 = n × e1; n = ICRF z when |r × v| < 1e-9 |r||v|), focus `:earth`, az −45°, el 30°, distance and target 2.5 × max(apoapsis radius, |r|) (`|r|` for a hyperbola, from `state->orbit` with μ⊕), clamped; `(map-view-cycle-focus! view)` (Tab): `:earth` ↔ `:ship`, keeping basis, az, el, distance, clamped to `(map-min-distance focus)` (50 m ship, 1.2 R⊕ Earth) and `*map-max-distance*` 1.5×10^13 m; `(map-view-zoom! view factor)`: target × factor, clamped (wheel 1.2^(−notches), Page-up 1/10, Page-down 10); `(map-view-drag! view dx dy)`: az −= 0.25° dx, el −= 0.25° dy, el clamped to ±85° (`decision 82`''s signs); `(map-camera-update! camera view render-state elapsed)`: log easing of the distance with τ `*map-zoom-tau*` 0.15 s (snap when elapsed is nil), anchor `:earth` or `:ship`, offset = distance × (cos el cos az e1 + cos el sin az e2 + sin el n), orientation looking at the focus with n''s projection as up, vertical FOV `*map-fov*` 50°. Conses nothing.
