INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (21, 2, 'Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel', 400, 'Part 9 of `plan 2: masterplan`: what the pilot reads and what happens at death. `overlay.lisp` grows from part 4''s placeholder label into the minimal flight readout of `docs/design.md` "Instruments" (the milestone-2 rows), its alarms and the clock''s warp messages, in the outside and map views; the death view (outside, camera kept, 3 s orange glow) and the "LOST: CRASH" panel follow a crash, and Return and N restart from the start state. It builds on `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events` (the clock''s level, actual rate, pause, messages and prediction; `sim-loss`; `clock-restart!` with the start-state checkpoint), `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets` (the overlay pass after the tone map, `render-state`, `capture-state`, `main.lisp`''s game and frame), `plan 18: The Mule''s meshes` (the ship''s per-frame emissive slot), `plan 19: Input and the outside view` (`*key-map*`, the input state, gating while lost, `outside-view-reset!`) and `plan 20: The basic map` (the completed glyph table, `label-at!`, `game-view`). It removes `PLACEHOLDER(80)`.

## Sources and decisions
- Specification: `docs/design.md` "Scope" → "Feature list": "Minimal readout (overlay): the `milestone 2` rows of "Instruments"" and "LOST panel, restart from the start state (in memory)" (both must, 2); the sections "Instruments" (the rows marked 2), "Time warp" (the warp field, actual rate, PAUSED, the message texts), "Dying and what follows" ("What the player sees", "What follows"), "Readability at 1280 × 800" (sizes, colours, "never colour alone"), "Views".
- Files and load order: `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" (`decision 12: Module layout and package split`): `overlay.lisp` (extended, after `post.lisp`), `render.lisp`, `input.lisp`, `main.lisp`, `capture.lisp` (extended); tests `tests/overlay.lisp` (created by `plan 20`''s piece 3 or here, before `tests/render.lisp`), `tests/render.lisp`, `tests/input.lisp`, `tests/capture.lisp`.
- Decisions: `decision 7: Placeholder labels: dot-matrix overlay quads`, `decision 34: How death works`, `decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering` (message texts), `decision 74: Crash test on the step''s Hermite and the death state` (the loss record), `decision 75: Prediction in milestone 2: the step function on a copy` (the `:impact` event), `decision 76: Frame passes, radiance scale and exposure` (stage 3, the radiance scale), `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 80: The Mule''s meshes in numbers: geometry, draws, materials and lights` (the emissive slot), `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 84: Map ribbons and markers: osculating orbit, adaptive segments, overlay markers and visibility` (the impact time is the readout''s), `decision 66: Calendar dates on the 1/64 s grid` (display truncates to seconds), `decision 49: Story: names, call signs and ships`.
- Recorded for this plan: `decision 85: Minimal readout: layout, formats, colours and alarms`, `decision 86: Death view, LOST panel and restart in milestone 2`.
- From part 1 (`plan 13`): `state->orbit`, `orbit-…` apsides, `format-utc`, the km and km/s conversions, the duration fields, R⊕, μ⊕, the crash radii. From part 2 (`plan 14`): the `controls` fields (throttle, mode, hold kind, settled, fine). From part 3 (`plan 15`): `clock-level`, `clock-actual-rate`, `clock-paused`, `clock-messages`, the clock''s `prediction` and `prediction-event`, `sim-loss` and the loss struct (cause, body, t, speed, latitude, longitude), `clock-restart!`.
- Tests: `docs/architecture.md` "Testing" → "Rules for tests", "Warp, events and collisions" → "Checkpoints" (a death followed by Return restores the latest checkpoint), "GPU tests" (image checks, never pixel-exact except the overlay''s exact colours).

## Rules for every piece
- The readout''s and the panel''s contents are pure functions (no GPU) of the render state, the clock, the loss and the real time, tested in `tests/overlay.lisp` without a canvas; only drawing touches the HAL. Nothing here changes the sim except `game-restart!` through `clock-restart!`.
- Text is drawn with the one glyph table and `label-at!` of `plan 20`; colours, sizes, the glow''s numbers and the panel''s place are `defparameter`s citing `decision 85` or `decision 86`, so `./sly eval` retunes them on the next frame.
- The overlay''s per-frame vertex data through the frame resource cache of part 4 (never one buffer rewritten while the previous frame reads it), its capacity a `defparameter` sized for the readout, the map''s labels and the panel together; text past it is cut, never a crash.
- The readout''s formatting may cons (strings per frame), measured: one frame''s readout conses under 16 KB.
- Each piece passes `scripts/test` (under ~15 s) and keeps `AGENTS.md` "Layout" and `docs/` true; no luv gap is expected, one met goes to `docs/luv-capabilities.md` and `docs/luv-wishlist.md`.

## Pieces, in the order they run

### 1. The readout''s contents: rows, formats, alarms, messages (pure)
- `overlay.lisp`: `(readout-lines render-state clock real-time)` → a list of lines, each a list of runs (text, colour, style `:plain` or `:inverted`, flashing flag), as `decision 85` sets:
  - `ALT` |r| − R⊕ in km, one decimal; `SPD` |v| (Earth''s inertial frame), m/s with one decimal below 1,000 m/s, else km/s with three; `AP` / `PE` the osculating apsis altitudes (`state->orbit` with μ⊕) in km with one decimal, `AP ESCAPE` when e ≥ 1; `THR` the lever in whole % and `ON` (throttle > 0 and propellant > 0) or `OFF`; `PROP` whole kg and whole % of 28,000 kg; `MODE` `DIRECT`, `RATE DAMP` or `HOLD <kind>` with `SETTLED` / `SLEWING`, then `FINE`; `WARP ×<level>`, `ACT ×<rate>` (3 significant digits, amber, "!") when `clock-actual-rate` < 0.9 × nominal, `PAUSED`; `UTC` `format-utc` of t_r truncated to whole seconds.
  - Labels grey #8A8A80, values paper white #E8E4D8, cautions amber #FFB000 with "!", danger red #FF3030 inverted and flashing at 2 Hz of `real-time` (on in the first half of each 0.5 s).
  - Alarms: amber `! PE BELOW 100 KM` while the osculating periapsis radius is below R⊕ + 100 km; red inverted flashing `EARTH IMPACT IN <duration>` (`MOON …` for the Moon) while the clock''s prediction has an `:impact` event, the duration from t_r to its time.
  - Messages: `clock-messages` (3 s each, the clock''s real time), newest last, at most `*readout-messages*` 3, amber with "!", cut at 40 characters with "…".
- Durations: the text the clock''s warp messages use (`plan 15` piece 5); if `clock.lisp` formats it locally, move it to `units.lisp` as `(format-duration seconds)` and call it from both, so the readout and the messages agree.
- Glyphs (`decision 85`): add `% / ! + ( ) , ° × …` to `plan 20`''s table (A–Z, 0–9, space, `-`, `.`, `:`); `(glyph-missing string)` → the first character without a glyph or nil.
- Tests `tests/overlay.lisp` (CPU):
  - The start state (`new-game-sim`, a fresh clock at ×1): `ALT` 400.0 KM within the one-decimal rounding of |r| − R⊕ (400,000.0 m: 6,778,136.6 − 6,378,136.6), `SPD` the circular speed √(μ⊕/a) in km/s to three decimals (7.669), `AP` and `PE` both 400.0, `THR 0% OFF`, `PROP 28000 KG 100%`, `MODE HOLD PROGRADE SETTLED`, `WARP ×1`, `UTC 2040-01-01 00:00:00`; no alarm, no message.
  - Formats from crafted states: 950 m/s shows `950.0 M/S`, 1,000 m/s `1.000 KM/S`; e = 1.2 shows `AP ESCAPE`; throttle 0.45 with 0 kg shows `THR 45% OFF`, with propellant `THR 45% ON`; rate damping with fine shows `MODE RATE DAMP FINE`; a paused clock at ×1,000 shows `WARP ×1000 PAUSED`; a clock whose meter reads 490,000 at ×1,000,000 shows `ACT ×490000` amber with "!", one at 950,000 none.
  - Alarms: the 400 × 50 km orbit of `plan 15`''s hazards tests: `! PE BELOW 100 KM` amber; with the clock''s prediction run to completion, `EARTH IMPACT IN …` red, inverted, flashing, its duration matching the prediction''s impact time − t_r; flashing on at real time 0.1 s and off at 0.35 s.
  - Messages: a refused warp-up (throttle on at ×10) puts `! WARP REFUSED: ENGINE ON, LIMIT ×10` in the lines; after 3 s of the clock''s real time it is gone; a 60-character message is cut to 40 with "…".
  - Glyphs: `glyph-missing` is nil for every string of every line above, for the clock''s refusal and lowering messages produced in `tests/clock.lisp`''s cases, and for "RCS OFF ABOVE ×4".
  - Allocation: one `readout-lines` call conses under 16 KB.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "Instruments": a short bullet list after the table with the milestone-2 rows as `decision 85` lays them out (labels, units, decimals, alarms, where the impact time comes from).
- Done: the tests pass; `./sly eval ''(readout-lines …)'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` on the live game prints the rows.

### 2. Drawing the readout in the overlay pass
- `overlay.lisp`: `(readout-vertices! out lines x y)`: the opaque #0A0C0C box sized to the lines, then each run through `label-at!` with the 2 px dot pitch, 12 × 22 px cells and 16 px margin of `decision 85`; an inverted run draws its colour block and the text in #0A0C0C; a flashing run in its off phase draws nothing. Top left in `:outside` and `:map` (`game-view`), after the map''s markers and labels.
- `render.lisp`: the overlay pass draws the readout from the frame''s render state, the clock and the game''s real time (summed elapsed, kept by `main.lisp`); the `PLACEHOLDER(76 77 80)` label loses 80 (or goes, if parts 5 and 6 have removed theirs); `PLACEHOLDER(80)` removed from code, `docs/` and `AGENTS.md`.
- `capture.lisp`: `capture-state` takes `:readout` (default t). Every GPU test of earlier parts is re-run: where a region check now falls under the readout box, that test passes `:readout nil` (named in its comment) rather than moving its bounds.
- Tests `tests/render.lisp` (GPU, in the existing `with-capture-game`, 1280 × 800 for this check or the size the other checks use if the box fits): the start state''s capture has, inside the readout box''s computed rectangle, only pixels of exactly #0A0C0C, #8A8A80 and #E8E4D8 (the overlay is after the tone map, `decision 76`), and at least one pixel of each; with `:readout nil` that rectangle shows the scene (some pixel not #0A0C0C); `report-failed-live-artifacts` 0.
- Docs: `AGENTS.md` "Layout" (`src/`: the readout in `overlay.lisp`), "Commands" → Screenshot: the PNG shows the readout; `docs/architecture.md` "GPU tests" (`capture-state`''s `:readout`).
- Done: the tests pass; `scripts/screenshot /tmp/r.png` shows the readout top left, legible, over the scene (the agent looks at the PNG); in `./sly play` a `./sly eval` of `(clock-warp-up …)` twice shows `WARP ×10` in the next `./sly screenshot`; the frame time with the readout noted in the done note (not a gate).

### 3. Death view, LOST panel, Return and N
- `main.lisp` (`decision 86`): the game keeps its summed real time, the loss last seen and the real time of the death; on the first frame with a new `sim-loss`, `game-view` becomes `:outside` (the outside view''s offset unchanged, so the camera stays put around the stopped ship) and the death time is recorded. `(game-restart! game)`: `clock-restart!` with the start-state checkpoint, `:outside`, `outside-view-reset!`, the map view closed, the input''s held keys, taps and drag cleared, the death record cleared, the exposure snapped.
- Glow: `(death-glow-radiance loss seconds-since-death)` (pure) → `*death-glow-radiance*` 4.0 for t ≤ 1 s, linear to 0 at 3 s, 0 after and for a Moon impact; the renderer writes `*death-glow-colour*` #FF6A1A × that ÷ the current exposure into `plan 18`''s per-frame emissive slot.
- `overlay.lisp`: `(lost-panel-lines loss)` (pure): `LOST: CRASH` red inverted, `<EARTH|MOON>  <UTC of the impact>`, `SPEED <as SPD>`, `LAT <|lat|>° <N|S>  LON <|lon|>° <E|W>` (2 decimals), a blank line, `RETURN  RESTART FROM START`, `N       NEW GAME`; drawn with the readout''s text on an opaque box centred horizontally, top at `*lost-panel-top*` 0.6 of the height; the readout stays.
- `input.lisp`: `*key-map*` binds `:return` and `:n` to `:restart` while `sim-lost-p` (N stays translate-back otherwise; flight keys are ignored while lost, `decision 81`); `:restart` calls `game-restart!`. M, the mouse and quit still act.
- `capture.lisp`: `capture-state` of a lost sim draws the glow at `:death-elapsed` (default 0, the peak) and the panel, so part 10''s `deorbit` screenshot shows the crash.
- Tests:
  - `tests/overlay.lisp`: a loss record built by `plan 15`''s radial free fall (Earth) gives `LOST: CRASH`, `EARTH`, the speed as the readout formats it, latitude and longitude from the record with hemisphere letters; a Moon loss gives `MOON`; `glyph-missing` nil for all; `death-glow-radiance` 4.0 at 0 and 1 s, 2.0 at 2 s, 0 at 3 s and 10 s within 1e-12, 0 for the Moon.
  - `tests/input.lisp` (synthetic events, no canvas): not lost, N is a held translation key and Return does nothing; lost, W and 1 change nothing, Return calls the restart; after a restart by N, the next `input-frame!` holds no key (no translation command in the controls).
  - `tests/render.lisp` or `tests/input.lisp` (no GPU): a game started from the `plan 15` deorbit state run through `clock-frame!` to the impact, then frames: the view becomes `:outside` from `:map`, the outside view''s offset unchanged; `game-restart!` gives a sim `equalp` to `(new-game-sim)` at ×1 unpaused, the view `:outside` with the default outside camera; 1,000 frames of 1/60 s after it equal 1,000 frames after a fresh game bit for bit; N and Return give the same sim (`decision 34`: in milestone 2 they are the same).
  - `tests/render.lisp` (GPU): the capture of a lost sim at the impact (the deorbit case of `plan 15`) has the panel box''s rectangle in exact #0A0C0C, #FF3030 (the inverted title), #E8E4D8 and #8A8A80 only; the ship''s pixels at `:death-elapsed` 0 are redder (mean R − B) than at 3.5 s by a margin set from the frame.
- Docs: `docs/design.md` "Dying and what follows" → "What the player sees": the glow''s curve, the panel''s lines and place, Return and N in milestone 2, the camera that may still be orbited (`decision 86`); "Controls": Return and N while lost; `docs/architecture.md` "Checkpoints": `game-restart!` is the restore the LOST panel calls; `AGENTS.md` "Commands" → Run: after a crash, Return or N restarts.
- Done: the tests pass; in `./sly play`, `./sly eval` setting the deorbit state (or a 200 s retrograde burn) and warping to the impact shows, in `./sly screenshot`s, the orange glow and the panel, and a synthetic Return brings back the start state with the readout at `ALT 400.0 KM`; `scripts/test` stays under ~15 s (measured, in the done note).

## What later parts take from here
- Part 10 (`flights.lisp`, `scripts/fly`): `capture-state`''s `:readout` and `:death-elapsed` for each `:screenshot`; the `deorbit` script''s last screenshot shows the panel; `readout-lines` values as a cross-check of the script records (altitude, apsides).
- Milestone 3: the overlay''s message line and the autopilot panel (`overlay.lisp`), the readout kept in the outside view while the cockpit screens carry the full set; the latest checkpoint for Return, N a fresh `(new-game-sim)`; contact''s white flash through the same emissive slot and `death-glow-radiance`''s case.
- Milestone 4: `LOST: HEAT` and `LOST: LIFE SUPPORT` panels and their effects (the ship''s lights out) as further cases of `lost-panel-lines` and the glow function.', '2026-10-14T22:48:59Z', 80);
INSERT INTO plan (id, milestone_id, subject, priority, body, created_at, created_by_task) VALUES (22, 2, 'Flight scripts and the Done when', 250, 'Part 10 of `plan 2: masterplan`: flight scripts and the milestone''s Done when. `flights.lisp`, the last simulation file, reads a script (`flights/<name>.sexp`), applies its actions through the same `controls` and clock commands the keys use, waits on the prediction''s events and on conditions, records checkpoints, expectations and failures, and runs headless (`run-flight`) or in the live game (`fly`). The three milestone-2 scripts `burn`, `raise-orbit` and `deorbit` are tested headless in `scripts/test`, and `scripts/fly <name> <out-dir>` renders a PNG per `:screenshot`. The last piece is the milestone''s Done when, checked from a clean checkout. It builds on every earlier part: `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`, `plan 14: Ship, integrator and flight computer`, `plan 15: Clock, warp, hazards and events`, `plan 16: Rendering foundation and assets`, `plan 17: Earth, Moon, Sun and stars`, `plan 18: The Mule''s meshes`, `plan 19: Input and the outside view`, `plan 20: The basic map` and `plan 21: Minimal readout, messages and the LOST panel`; it runs after all of them, since its screenshots need the whole picture.

## Sources and decisions
- Specification: `docs/design.md` "Scope" → "Feature list": "Flight scripts `burn`, `raise-orbit`, `deorbit` with screenshots" (must, 2); "Each milestone against its Outcome and Done when" (`milestone 2`: "the Done when''s raise and deorbit are the flight scripts"); "The start" (the polar 400 km orbit, `decision 38: Start orbit: polar`); "The ship(s)" (RL10C-1 class: 101.8 kN, v_e 4,410 m/s; wet 35,961 kg); "Dying and what follows".
- Architecture: `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs" (Steps, Actions, Waits and expectations, Start states, Running scripts, Scripts by milestone), "Determinism", "Checkpoints", "Testing" → "Rules for tests" and "Warp, events and collisions" ("Determinism: the same flight script run twice gives bit-identical states"), "Files in load order" (`flights.lisp` after `prediction.lisp` in milestone 2), "Dev loop" (live-redefinable code).
- Decisions: `decision 21: Physics test bounds and flight scripts`, `decision 56: Flight-script actions, start states and the quest play-through`, `decision 72: Simulation state and the one step function in clock.lisp`, `decision 73: Warp levels above x4: entry, holds and lowering`, `decision 74: Crash test on the step''s Hermite and the death state`, `decision 75: Prediction in milestone 2: the step function on a copy`, `decision 77: The frame in main.lisp: render state, capture of a given sim, part 4''s placeholders and first asset`, `decision 81: Input in milestone 2: held keys per frame, taps, gating and the shared key map`, `decision 86: Death view, LOST panel and restart in milestone 2`, `decision 66: Calendar dates on the 1/64 s grid`, `decision 64: Scripts always re-enter the dev shell`, `decision 10: Test and screenshot commands`, `decision 34: How death works`.
- Recorded for this plan: `decision 87: Flight scripts in milestone 2: additions, apsis conditions, live fly and scripts/fly` (the safe reader; `(:restart)`, `(:expect :start-state)`, `(:expect :impact-as-predicted <s>)`, `:before` on event waits, `:view :map` on screenshots; apsis conditions on the prediction''s apsides; one per-step function for headless and live; the scripts'' numbers; live `fly`; what `scripts/fly` writes in milestone 2; screenshots not committed).
- From part 1 (`plan 13`): `+fine-step+`, `grid-ceiling`, `utc->grid-t`, `format-utc`, R⊕, μ⊕, the crash radius, `state->orbit` (the osculating periapsis at an impact). From part 2 (`plan 14`): the `controls-…` commands (holds, throttle lever, fine), the odometer, `controls-apply-held-keys!` (`plan 19`''s piece in `controls.lisp`). From part 3 (`plan 15`): `sim`, `copy-sim`, `new-game-sim`, `sim-step!` with `until`, the `cutoff` slot, `sim-loss`, the `clock` with its `hook`, `clock-warp-up` / `-down` / `-reset`, refusal messages, `clock-restart!`, the prediction (`prediction-update!`, `prediction-run!`, `prediction-event`). From parts 4, 8 and 9 (`plan 16`, `plan 20`, `plan 21`): `capture-state` with `:view`, `:readout`, `:death-elapsed`, `camera-fn`; `with-capture-game`; `game-restart!`. From part 7 (`plan 19`): `input-frame!` and its gating.

## Rules for every piece
- `flights.lisp` is simulation code: it never calls the HAL or SDL; `fly` touches only the `game` object''s clock, sim and view state, and `scripts/fly`''s captures go through `capture.lisp`.
- Live-redefinable (`docs/architecture.md` "Dev loop"): the hook given to the clock is a lambda calling the named `flight-step-hook`; the running flight''s state lives in a slot of `game` (`:initform nil`), headless in a `flight` struct; tunables (`*flight-default-within*` 30 days, the coast''s caps) are `defparameter`s.
- Determinism: no wall clock, no hash-table iteration order; every time from a script is rounded to the 1/64 s grid (`grid-ceiling` for relative times, `utc->grid-t` for dates); headless and live take the same steps (`decision 87`).
- Physics tests stay under ~5 s together and `scripts/test` under ~15 s; this part''s headless tests under 1.5 s (measured, in the done note). No GPU in `tests/flights.lisp`.
- Each piece adds its files to `luv-in-space.asd` (`tests/flights.lisp` last among the simulation tests, before `tests/render.lisp`), passes `scripts/test`, and keeps `AGENTS.md` ("Commands", "Layout") and `docs/architecture.md` ("Files in load order", "Scripted runs") true. A luv gap met goes to `docs/luv-capabilities.md` and `docs/luv-wishlist.md`.

## Pieces, in the order they run

### 1. Reading scripts and `run-flight` (headless): actions, waits, expectations, the record
- `clock.lisp` (extends part 3''s file): if `clock-frame!` keeps the per-step body inline, factor it out as `(clock-step! clock sim)` (the lowering rules of `decision 73`, the hook with its `until`, `sim-step!`), called by `clock-frame!` unchanged in behaviour (part 3''s clock tests stay green, bit for bit).
- `prediction.lisp` (extends): `(prediction-apsis pred kind)` → time and radius of the next predicted `:apoapsis` or `:periapsis` from the stored Hermite, or, with an `:impact` before it, the osculating apsis of the impact state (`decision 87`); add it only if part 3 has no equivalent.
- `flights.lisp` (new, after `prediction.lisp`):
  - Reader (`decision 87`): `(read-flight pathname-or-string)`: `*read-eval*` nil, `*read-default-float-format*` `double-float`, `*package*` a scratch package deleted after; exactly one form; any symbol not a keyword, or a second form, rejected with a `flight-script-error` naming the line; then each step is parsed into a step struct: unknown keywords and those of later milestones (`:target`, `:autopilot`, `:grapple`, `:release`, `:transfer`, `:translate`, `:approach`, `:ack`, `:start :state` / `:after` / `:file`, quest conditions, …) rejected at read time with "NOT BEFORE MILESTONE <n>" (the milestone of the "Actions" table and "Waits and expectations"). `flights/<name>.sexp` resolved against the system''s source directory (`asdf:system-relative-pathname`), so the packaged build and `./sly` find them.
  - Timing (`docs/architecture.md` "Steps"): `:at` from the script''s start, `:after` from the previous step''s end, a bare action `:after 0`; `(:after 300)` alone lets time pass; every time to the grid.
  - Actions of milestone 2: `(:start :new-game)` (also when absent; `new-game-sim`), `(:warp <level>)` (repeated `clock-warp-up` / `-down` to the level; a refusal ends the script, failed, with the clock''s message as reason), `(:warp :coast)` (from then on, in the hook before each step, raise to the highest level the clock accepts; `(:warp 1)` ends it), `(:hold <mode>)` (`:prograde` … `:inertial`, `nil` to rate damping), `(:throttle <f>)` (0 or 0.1–1.0), `(:after-dv <m/s> :throttle 0)` (arms the sim''s `cutoff` at the odometer plus the value, so the cut lands exactly as `decision 72` sets), `(:keys (<key> …) :for <s>)` (`controls-apply-held-keys!` on, then off after the time), `(:fine <t/nil>)`, `(:screenshot "<label>" [:view :map])` (a copy of the sim and the view in the record), `(:restart)` (`decision 87`: only while lost; headless `clock-restart!` with the run''s start state).
  - Waits: events `:apoapsis`, `:periapsis`, `:impact` (from the prediction, run to completion before the wait; the wait passes the event''s grid time, less `:before <s>`, to `sim-step!` as `until`; `:impact` remembers the predicted time for `:impact-as-predicted`); conditions tested after each step: `:altitude-below`, `:periapsis-below` / `-above`, `:apoapsis-below` / `-above` (the prediction''s apsides, `decision 87`), `:crashed`, `:settled`, `:rate-below <°/s>`, `:date "<UTC>"` (exact on the grid), `:propellant-above <kg>`, `:propellant-full`, `:drop-out :impact`; every wait has `:within <s>` (default 30 days of game time).
  - Expectations: the same conditions now, plus `:lost :crash`, `:impact-as-predicted <s>`, `:start-state` (`decision 87`); a failed one is recorded and the script goes on.
  - Failure (`docs/architecture.md` "Steps"): a wait out of time, a refused action, or a death not expected by a following `(:expect :lost :crash)` ends the script, failed, with the reason and the state; a death while the next step is `(:expect :lost :crash)` is not a failure.
  - The record: per `:screenshot` and `:expect`, per burn (throttle on to off: start, end, Δv from the odometer), per failure, and at the end: `t` (and UTC), altitude, apoapsis, periapsis, speed, propellant, the loss; `(flight-record-lines record)` prints one line each, as `scripts/fly` will.
  - `(run-flight script &key model)`: the start state, a fresh clock, then `prediction-update!` and `clock-step!` per step with the hook applying the actions (headless warp sets only the step, the thrust limits, refusals and drop-outs; "3 s of real time" at the nominal level, `docs/architecture.md` "Running scripts"); `:model` overrides the sim''s gravity model (`:point` for the two-body check of piece 2); returns the record and the end sim.
- Tests `tests/flights.lisp` (CPU, scripts as strings):
  - Reader: `#.` (read-eval) rejected; a non-keyword symbol rejected; two forms rejected; `(:autopilot …)` rejected with "NOT BEFORE MILESTONE 3"; `9.10`-style floats read as doubles.
  - Timing: `(:at 0.01 …)` lands on 0 or 1/64 s by `grid-ceiling`; `(:after 300)` alone advances `t` by exactly 300 s from the previous step''s end.
  - Cut-off: `(:throttle 1.0) (:after-dv 25.0 :throttle 0)` at ×1 and under `(:warp :coast)`: the odometer at the cut within the fine step''s Δv (×1) and on the closed form (coast, ×100), `t` on the grid; the apoapsis after it within 1 m between the two (as `plan 15`''s prediction test).
  - Waits: `(:wait :apoapsis)` from the start orbit with a small prograde burn ends at the first grid point at or after the predicted time; `:before 10` ends 10 s earlier on the grid; `(:wait :date "2040-01-01T01:00:00")` ends with `t` equal to `utc->grid-t` of it; a wait with `:within 10` that cannot hold fails the script with the wait in the reason.
  - Refusal: `(:throttle 1.0) (:warp 1000)` fails with "WARP REFUSED: ENGINE ON, LIMIT x10" (the clock''s text).
  - Keys: `(:keys (:w) :for 2)` from the prograde hold releases it to rate damping and the pitch rate after 2 s is non-zero, then damped.
  - Death: a radial free fall start (built in the test by setting the sim, not a script action) followed by `(:wait :impact)` without an `:expect` fails with cause `:crash`; with `(:expect :lost :crash)` next it passes; `(:restart)` then `(:expect :start-state)` passes.
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs": "Actions" gains `(:restart)` (2) and `:view` on `:screenshot`; "Waits and expectations" gains `:before` on event waits, `:start-state`, `:impact-as-predicted`, and the note that apsis conditions read the prediction''s apsides (`decision 87`); "Running scripts": `clock-step!`, `run-flight`''s `:model`, `--from` and `<name>.end.sexp` with `saves.lisp` (milestone 5). "Files in load order": `flights.lisp` exists. `AGENTS.md` "Layout" (`src/`: `flights.lisp`).
- Done: the tests pass; `./sly eval ''(run-flight "((:throttle 1.0) (:after 10 :throttle 0) (:expect :apoapsis-above 450e3))")'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` prints a passing record.

### 2. The three milestone-2 scripts, headless and deterministic
- `flights/burn.sexp`: from the start state at ×1: `(:screenshot "before")`, `(:after 10 :throttle 1.0)`, `(:after 5 :screenshot "during")` (engine glow, `plan 18`''s "should" if built), `(:after 5 :throttle 0)` (10 s, about 28.4 m/s: m 35,961 → 35,730 kg at ṁ 23.08 kg/s), expects the apoapsis about 500 km (the closed form from the burn''s Δv, a band of ±10 km for J2 and the finite burn, measured and set by the worker), the periapsis 380–405 km, propellant 27,769 kg within 5 kg (230.8 kg by the engine, a little by the hold''s RCS); `(:screenshot "after" :view :map)`.
- `flights/raise-orbit.sexp` (`decision 87`), Hohmann 400 → 800 km: `(:warp :coast)`, `(:screenshot "start" :view :map)`, `(:throttle 1.0)`, `(:after-dv 109.1 :throttle 0)` (≈ 38 s), expects apoapsis 792–808 km and periapsis 385–405 km, `(:screenshot "transfer" :view :map)`; `(:wait :apoapsis :before <half the second burn>)` (107.6 m/s at ≈ 35,083 kg: ≈ 37 s, so `:before 18.5`, the worker refines from the flight), `(:throttle 1.0)`, `(:after-dv 107.6 :throttle 0)`, expects both apsides 792–808 km (1 % of the 800 km apsis altitude; widened with a comment if J2''s wobble needs it, measured), `(:screenshot "raised" :view :map)`, `(:screenshot "raised-outside")`.
- `flights/deorbit.sexp`: `(:hold :retrograde)`, `(:wait :settled :within 120)`, `(:screenshot "retrograde")`, `(:warp :coast)`, `(:throttle 1.0)`, `(:after-dv 102.3 :throttle 0)` (periapsis 50 km, 50 km below the crash radius, as `plan 15`''s crash test), `(:expect :periapsis-below 100e3)`, `(:screenshot "falling" :view :map)` (the red arc and the impact marker of `plan 20`), `(:wait :altitude-below 150e3)`, `(:screenshot "entry")`, `(:wait :impact)`, `(:expect :lost :crash)`, `(:expect :impact-as-predicted 0.1)`, `(:screenshot "lost")` (glow at its peak and the LOST panel, `plan 21`), `(:restart)`, `(:expect :start-state)`, `(:screenshot "restarted")`.
- Each script file starts with a comment block: what it shows, the closed-form numbers behind its Δv and bands (μ⊕, R⊕ + 400 km = 6,778,136.6 m, v_e 4,410 m/s), and that `scripts/fly <name> <dir>` renders it.
- Tests `tests/flights.lisp`:
  - Each script headless: no failure, every expectation passes; the burn''s and the deorbit''s death and restart as above.
  - Determinism (`docs/architecture.md` "Warp, events and collisions"): each script run twice gives `equalp` end sims and equal records (every double bit for bit).
  - The raise''s 1 % (`decision 87`): `raise-orbit` with `:model :point` (two-body; the script''s apsis bands replaced by the test) gives both final apsides at 800 km ± 4 km, i.e. the planned 400 km raise within 1 %, and the transfer''s apoapsis likewise.
  - The deorbit''s impact time within 0.1 s of the prediction taken when `(:wait :impact)` began (the script''s own expect), and its point''s latitude and longitude in the record.
  - Run time of all three scripts twice plus the two-body run under 1 s (measured in the done note; physics stays under ~5 s).
- Docs: `docs/architecture.md` "Scripts by milestone" → `milestone 2`: each script''s steps and numbers as built (the raise''s two-body check, the full-model bands, the deorbit''s restart).
- Done: the tests pass; `./sly eval ''(flight-record-lines (run-flight "deorbit"))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` prints the burns, the impact and the restart.

### 3. `fly` live and `scripts/fly` with screenshots
- `flights.lisp`: `(fly name &key (game *game*))` (`decision 87`): restores the game to the script''s start state as `game-restart!` does (`plan 21`), keeps the flight in the game''s `flight` slot, installs the clock hook (a lambda calling `flight-step-hook`), returns at once; the script then runs frame by frame through `clock-frame!`, the same `clock-step!` as headless; at its end (or a failure) the hook is removed and the record printed to the image''s output; `(flight-status &key (game *game*))` returns the record lines so far; `(flight-stop)` removes the hook. `(:restart)` live calls `game-restart!`.
- `input.lisp` (extends `plan 19`''s file): while the game has a running flight, `input-frame!` writes no held keys and runs no ramp, and the flight keys are ignored as when lost (`decision 81`, `decision 87`); warp keys are ignored too (the script owns warp); P, C, Home, M, Tab, Page keys, the mouse and quit act.
- `capture.lisp` (extends): `(fly-screenshots record out-dir)` renders each `:screenshot` checkpoint''s sim with `capture-state` (its `:view`, the default outside pose, `:death-elapsed` 0 for a lost sim) inside one `with-capture-game`, as `<out-dir>/<n>-<label>.png` with `n` two digits from 01; `(fly-main name out-dir)` (the entry of `scripts/fly`): `run-flight`, the record lines on stdout, the PNGs, exit 1 on a failure or a missing script.
- `scripts/fly` (new, like `scripts/screenshot`: re-enters the dev shell unless `LIS_DEV_SHELL=1`, `decision 64`; usage `scripts/fly <name> <out-dir>`, exit 2 on bad arguments): loads `luv-in-space`, calls `fly-main`; headless on lavapipe without a display.
- Tests: `tests/flights.lisp` (CPU): `burn` flown through `clock-frame!` with a game-less clock fed simulated frames of 1/60 s, and again of irregular elapsed times (a fixed list), gives the same end sim (`equalp`) and record as `run-flight` (`docs/architecture.md` "Running scripts": the same states bit for bit); `tests/input.lisp`: with a flight running, W and Shift change no control; `tests/capture.lisp` (GPU, in the existing `with-capture-game`): `fly-screenshots` of `burn`''s record writes three PNGs of 1280 × 800 with the PNG signature and no fully black frame, in a temporary directory, deleted after.
- Docs: `AGENTS.md` "Commands": `scripts/fly <name> <out-dir>` (what it writes, exit codes, the time measured), "Live image": `./sly eval ''(fly "raise-orbit")'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE`, `(flight-status)`, keys ignored while a flight runs; "Layout": `flights/` and `scripts/fly`; `docs/architecture.md` "Running scripts" as built.
- Done: the tests pass; `scripts/fly raise-orbit /tmp/fly-raise` writes the five PNGs and exits 0 (the agent looks at them: the ring, the transfer ellipse with AP near 800 km, the raised ring, the ship outside), the directory then deleted; in `./sly start` / `./sly play`, `./sly eval ''(fly "burn")''` and a `./sly screenshot` during the burn shows the engine on and `THR 100 % ON`; `./sly stop`.

### 4. The Done when from a clean checkout
- Not code: the milestone''s Done when (`milestone 2`, `docs/design.md` "Each milestone against its Outcome and Done when"), checked by an agent; anything that fails becomes a follow-up task (`pm task add` in the plan of the part that owns it) and this task stays open until those are done, or is dropped with the reason.
- From a clean checkout: `git clone` of this repo into a temporary directory (no `build/`, no `result`), then there: `nix build` (time noted), `scripts/test` (passes, time under ~15 s, noted), `nix flake check` (passes), `scripts/fly burn`, `raise-orbit` and `deorbit` into a temporary directory (exit 0; the agent looks at every PNG: the ship and Earth outside, the map''s ring and ellipses, the impact marker and red arc, the glow and `LOST: CRASH`, the restarted start), `scripts/screenshot` (the start state with the readout).
- Once live: `./sly start`, `./sly play`, `./sly eval ''(fly "raise-orbit")''` and `./sly screenshot`s at the first burn and after the raise, then `(fly "deorbit")` to the LOST panel, a synthetic Return (as `plan 21`''s piece 3 does) and a screenshot of the start state; `./sly stop`. Then `nix run` started in the background, closed by its PID (`kill $!`) after a few seconds: the window opens without error. No process left running.
- By hand, as a player, once (the Outcome''s "the player flies it by hand"): in `./sly play`, synthetic key events through `./sly eval` (prograde hold, Shift to raise the throttle, X to cut, warp up and down, M and Tab), each followed by a `./sly screenshot`, the readout''s values moving as expected.
- Docs against what was built: `AGENTS.md` ("Commands": every command listed runs as written with the times stated; "Layout": every file and directory; the `src/` bullet no longer says walking skeleton or `PLACEHOLDER(23)`); `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order" against `luv-in-space.asd` and `src/`, "Testing" against `tests/` (each named test exists or its row says which milestone writes it), "Scripted runs" against `flights.lisp`; `docs/design.md` "Feature list": every milestone-2 must row built, each should row built or noted as not built with a follow-up task; `grep -rn ''PLACEHOLDER('' src tests` lists only tasks of later milestones (each id checked with `pm show`); `docs/luv-capabilities.md` and `docs/luv-wishlist.md` list the luv gaps met in milestone 2.
- The screenshots are not committed (`decision 87`); the done note lists the commands and the times measured. Temporary clones and directories deleted.
- Done: every check above passes, or each failure has a follow-up task named in the done note; the done note of this task is the milestone''s evidence.

## What later milestones take from here
- `milestone 3`: pilot actions, `(:start :state …)`, the terminal approach and the autopilot conditions in `flights.lisp`; their read-time rejections ("NOT BEFORE MILESTONE 3") become implementations; `scripts/fly` serves the preset and rendezvous scripts.
