- The plan body ("The cockpit"); `docs/design.md` as written so far (life-support module dimensions, eye point, instrument list and milestones, controls); `docs/luv-capabilities.md` ("Rendering", "HUD and instruments", "Orbit lines and markers", "Sun glare and brightness"); `docs/architecture.md` ("Files in load order": `text.lisp`, `meshes.lisp`, cockpit and instrument files).
- Binding, cite: `decision 3: luv ASDF systems the game depends on`, `decision 4: Depth strategy` (cockpit in the same pass), `decision 7: Placeholder labels: dot-matrix overlay quads`, `decision 11: Render pipelines are luv live shader pipelines`, `decision 15: Coordinate frames`.

## Write
- The DIY look and a layout as a list of panels with positions and sizes (m, FRD) relative to the eye point, enough to build the cockpit mesh from; the window and its frame.
- Each instrument of the "Flight" list: what it shows, how it is drawn (Slug text on an in-world screen texture, needle gauge mesh, lamp, dot-matrix display, orbit plot), update rate, milestone.
- Ghostty terminal screen: keep (what for, what it costs) or cut, with the reason; if kept, add a follow-up task in this plan for the decision extending `decision 3`.
- Interaction: switches by mouse or keys; flying from the cockpit alone (`milestone 3` outcome); what the outside view adds.
- Readability rules at 1280x800: minimum text size, contrast in sun and shadow, colour use.
- How messages and radio reach the player (screens, printer strip, lamp), named so `docs/story.md` can use them.
- Replace this section''s `PLACEHOLDER` line.

## Decisions to record (`pm decision record`)
- Cockpit instrument technology (Slug screens, gauges, lamps) and Ghostty in or out.
- The message channels the story may use.

## Done when
- The section is complete and agrees with "Flight" and the ship; the decisions are recorded and cited; `git add docs/design.md`.', '2026-10-14T17:58:38Z', '2026-10-14T18:28:35Z', 37, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (42, 10, 'Design: the places, with real data and Δv checked against the ship', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md (''The places''; start orbit now polar per decision 38; decisions 38-40; follow-ups task 47, task 48)', 'Fifth part of `plan 10: game design`: write the section "The places" in `docs/design.md`, as the plan body specifies.

## Read first
- The plan body ("The places"); `docs/design.md` as written so far (start orbit, the ship''s Δv table and refuelling, the Sun''s heat rule and its distance, autopilot presets, docking/towing); `docs/architecture.md` ("Units", "Ephemerides", "Rails", "Assets"); `docs/luv-capabilities.md` ("Spheres and planet surfaces", "Sun glare and brightness", "Instancing many objects", "Starfield").
- Binding, cite: `decision 13: Asset storage and attribution` (texture licences, SOURCE.md, size limits), `decision 14: Units and time epoch` (μ and radii only from there), `decision 17: Gravity model` (drag is the design''s option), `decision 18: Ephemerides` (game time before 2050-01-01), `decision 19: Time-warp rules` (places on rails).

## Write
- Earth: Blue Marble, atmosphere rim, night side and clouds (in or cut), drag (cut or exponential atmosphere, with the reason).
- 4 to 6 Earth-orbit points of interest (`milestone 3` presets): name, purpose, orbit elements and epoch (real ones from a named source and date read, e.g. a CelesTrak TLE; invented ones marked invented), Δv from the start orbit (computed), look.
- The Moon: texture source and licence (checked against `decision 13`), lunar orbits of interest, landing in or cut (per the ship), Δv for TLI and LOI.
- Near-Earth asteroids and the belt: real objects from JPL SBDB with designation and date read, how they are shown, the ship''s work there; Δv and Hohmann travel times.
- Planets in scope with Δv and travel times the ship can do (with refuelling where needed), their look and texture sources.
- The Sun: look, danger zone in AU from the chosen heat rule, warnings.
- A sources list with dates read.
- Check every destination''s Δv against the ship''s Δv table; where one isn''t reachable, change the plan (refuelling, cut) and say so.
- Replace this section''s `PLACEHOLDER` line. Data and calculations in `/tmp`; no assets are downloaded or committed here (asset work belongs to the milestone the scope table assigns it to); a texture licence still to check is a follow-up task in this plan.

## Decisions to record (`pm decision record`)
- Places in scope: Earth-orbit points of interest, the Moon (landing in or out), which asteroids, which planets.
- Drag in or out; Earth''s night side and clouds.

## Done when
- The section is complete with sources and dates; every destination''s Δv is checked against the ship''s; the decisions are recorded and cited; `git add docs/design.md`.', '2026-10-14T17:58:38Z', '2026-10-14T18:42:52Z', 37, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (43, 10, 'Design: scope table, read-through and what the story may use', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md (Scope; read-through fixes), docs/architecture.md (title.lisp); decisions 41, 42 (partly superseding 39)', 'Last part of `plan 10: game design`: write the section "Scope" in `docs/design.md` and read the whole document through against the other documents, as the plan body specifies.

## Read first
- The plan body ("Scope", "Done when"); all of `docs/design.md`; `docs/luv-capabilities.md`; `docs/architecture.md`; `docs/luv-wishlist.md`; `pm milestone show 1` … `6` (Outcomes and Done-whens); `pm decision list --answered` (all decisions the earlier tasks of this plan recorded).

## Write
- One prioritised table: feature, priority (must/should/could), milestone (2 flight core, 3 cockpit and autopilot, 4 the solar system, 5 story and quests, 6 release) or "cut", reason. Cover every feature named in the document and in `milestone 1`''s developer ideas (rugged ships, low-tech weapons, autopilot presets, Moon, belt, planets, Sun death, DIY cockpit, story), plus title screen, intro, controls help, credits screen (`decision 13: Asset storage and attribution`), README, performance target, saves, audio, gamepad.
- Weapons: in or cut (low-tech only, only if the story needs them).
- Check against each milestone''s Outcome and Done when (e.g. `milestone 2`: outside view, minimal readout, crash into Earth; `milestone 4`: Sun death tested; `milestone 5`: saves). Where the design wins inside a milestone''s intent, say so; a real contradiction with a milestone is a `pm decision add` (and this task stays done; the decision blocks nothing here).
- "What the story may use": a short list by milestone (2 to 5) for `task 12: write plan: story`: ship, places, message channels, mechanics.
- Read-through: names (modules as in `docs/architecture.md` "Files in load order"), figures and milestones agree across sections and with `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/luv-capabilities.md`; every decision the document relies on is cited; no `PLACEHOLDER` lines left in `docs/design.md`; style per `AGENTS.md`.
- Where `docs/architecture.md` must follow a design choice (e.g. a module the design adds), adjust it here, citing the decision.

## Decisions to record (`pm decision record`)
- Weapons in or out; the scope table as the milestones'' specification (one decision listing what each milestone gets and what is cut).

## Follow-ups
- Tasks for what the document reveals: an asset licence to check, a luv wishlist item (`docs/luv-wishlist.md`), an architecture section to adjust beyond this task; each in the plan it belongs to (`pm plan list`), not duplicating existing tasks.

## Done when
- The plan''s "Done when" holds: every feature has a milestone or a cut with a reason; every destination''s Δv is checked; the decisions are recorded; `git add docs/design.md` (and any changed doc).', '2026-10-14T17:58:38Z', '2026-10-14T18:46:28Z', 37, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (44, 10, 'Verify the sourced figures of docs/design.md "The ship(s)"', 'work', 'done', 610, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md: sources of ''Propulsion'' with URLs and dates read; all figures agree (RL10C-1 22,890 lbf/449.7 s/MR 5.5/420 lb, gimbal ±4° from NASA TM-87335, CECE 10 % 2006 and 8 % 2009, RCS 360 s between Aerojet 1984 and Lewis 1969 data, LH2 70.85 and LOX 1,141 kg/m³, Al 2219 2,840 kg/m³ and 150 MPa = cold weld yield 193 MPa / 1.29); nothing recomputed, decision 22 not superseded', '`task 38: Design: the game in one page and the ship(s)` wrote `docs/design.md` "The ship(s)" without web access, so its engine and material figures are named with their sources but were not re-read online. Check each against its source, record the URL and date read next to it in `docs/design.md`, and fix any figure that differs (recompute what depends on it: Δv, burn times, tank lengths, masses, inertia, the Δv table; formulas are in the document).

- RL10C-1: vacuum thrust 101.8 kN, Isp 449.7 s, mixture ratio 5.5, mass 190 kg, nozzle exit Ø 1.45 m, length ~2.2 m, gimbal ±4° (Aerojet Rocketdyne / L3Harris data sheet).
- NASA CECE deep throttling to ~10 % (Glenn Research Center reports, 2006–2010).
- Gaseous O2/H2 RCS thrusters: Isp 360 s at ~445 N class (NASA low-thrust H2/O2 thruster tests; ULA IVF papers by Zegler and Kutter).
- Densities: LH2 70.8 kg/m³, LOX 1,141 kg/m³ at their normal boiling points (NIST Chemistry WebBook).
- Al 2219 density 2,840 kg/m³ and the 150 MPa allowable used for wall thickness.

If a change moves a figure recorded in `decision 22: The player''s ship and its propulsion`, supersede it with `pm decision record` and say so in the task note. Done when every source in "Propulsion" has a URL and date read, and the numbers agree with them.', '2026-10-14T18:08:07Z', '2026-10-14T20:41:28Z', 38, 1);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (45, 10, 'Architecture: the integrator takes the full inertia tensor', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/architecture.md', '`docs/design.md` "The ship(s)" → "Inertia" (`task 38: Design: the game in one page and the ship(s)`) found that the tug''s cab on top makes its inertia tensor non-diagonal in body axes (I_xz up to 2.7×10⁴ kg m², principal axes tilted up to 11°), so `ship.lisp` gives the integrator the full symmetric tensor about the current centre of mass, with its inverse.

`docs/architecture.md` "Time and integration" → "Integrator" says "I ω̇ = τ − ω × I ω (Euler''s equations, principal axes, I from the current propellant load, held over a step)". Change "principal axes" to "the full inertia tensor in body axes, from `ship.lisp`", and in "Testing" → "Drift bounds" add to the rotation test a case with a non-diagonal tensor (e.g. the diag(1, 2, 3)×10⁴ tensor rotated 10° about y), same bounds. This is a refinement of `decision 16: Integrator and simulation clock`, not a change to it; add a `pm decision consequences 16 "…"` line. Done when the two sections say so and agree with `docs/design.md`.', '2026-10-14T18:08:08Z', '2026-10-14T18:46:51Z', 38, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (46, 10, 'Architecture: contact, berthing and life-support events in hazards and warp', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/architecture.md (Files in load order, Rails, Time warp, Collisions and the Sun, Checkpoints, Testing), docs/design.md (Time warp cites decision 43); decisions 43, 44; follow-up task 49', '`docs/design.md` "Flight" (task 40: `decision 33: Grapple tolerances, contact and berthing`, `decision 34: How death works`) adds simulation pieces that `docs/architecture.md` does not yet name. Bring the architecture in step; no game code.

- "Collisions and the Sun": contact between the ship (three boxes) and promoted objects (spheres or boxes from `places.lisp`), swept bounding-sphere test then boxes, at every step; bounce (restitution 0.3) at ≤ 1.0 m/s, death above; the grapple''s capture as a perfectly inelastic coupling into one stack. The design''s hull-temperature rule (T_eq with α 0.30, ε 0.85, q 100 W/m², τ 900 s) as the chosen one.
- "Time warp": drop-out events also for a predicted contact with a promoted object and the life-support alarms (30 and 7 days); the Sun hazard zone is the 0.551 AU warning distance. Check this stays within `decision 19: Time-warp rules`, or record an extension.
- "Rails": a berthed ship is held at its station''s fixture (fixed relative pose) instead of integrated; releasing returns it to integration with the station''s velocity.
- "Files in load order": `hazards.lisp` gains contact (milestone 3) and life support (milestone 4); checkpoints before `milestone 5` live in memory (a state snapshot), `saves.lisp` writes them from `milestone 5`.
- Tests in "Testing" for contact (capture inside tolerance, bounce, death above 1 m/s, momentum conserved in a capture) and for berthing.', '2026-10-14T18:19:14Z', '2026-10-14T18:51:03Z', 40, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (47, 10, 'Verify the sourced figures and asset licences of docs/design.md "The places"', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md (The places: SBDB element table, re-run Lambert scans, asset files/sizes/credits, Sources with URLs and dates)', '`task 42: Design: the places, with real data and Δv checked against the ship` wrote `docs/design.md` "The places" without web access (`decision 28: Web access for task 44: Verify the sourced figures of docs/design.md "The ship(s)"` is pending), so several sources are only named. Read each online and record URL and date read in "The places", "Sources"; correct figures that differ and re-run the Δv checks they feed (a throwaway script in /tmp, nothing committed).

- JPL Small-Body Database: full element sets (a, e, i, Ω, ω, M, epoch) for (469219) Kamoʻoalewa, (1) Ceres, (2) Pallas, (4) Vesta, (10) Hygiea, (341843) 2008 EV5; replace the remembered values. Re-check the Lambert conclusions for Kamoʻoalewa (cheapest round trip ~360 days, ~5.0 km/s via Highport; 9.0 km/s within 180 days) and 2008 EV5 with the read elements over 2040–2048 departures.
- NASA SVS "CGI Moon Kit" (LROC WAC colour mosaic, LOLA `ldem_4`): URL, resolution and file sizes (the 4096×2048 colour must fit ≤ 5 MB as JPEG, `decision 13: Asset storage and attribution`), the credit line the page asks for, and that NASA''s media guidelines cover it.
- NASA Black Marble 2016 ("Earth at Night") and NASA Visible Earth "Blue Marble: Clouds": URLs, versions ≤ 5 MB, credits and licence; the Blue Marble NG January (`200401`) 5400×2700 file name.
- U.S. Standard Atmosphere 1976 density at 400 km (~2.8×10⁻¹² kg/m³).
- Sharkey et al. 2021 (Kamoʻoalewa) citation; Tianwen-2''s launch date; the ISS''s planned deorbit (~2030).
- Blocked while web tools are denied to workers; runs after `decision 28` is answered.', '2026-10-14T18:42:31Z', '2026-10-14T19:19:31Z', 42, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (48, 10, 'Architecture: rails across spheres of influence, hyperbolic rails and re-entry of released objects', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/architecture.md (Rails: hyperbolic rails, rails across spheres of influence, re-entry of objects; module list; tests; polar start orbit), docs/design.md (references); decision 46: Rails across spheres, hyperbolas and re-entry', '`docs/design.md` "The places" (`task 42: Design: the places, with real data and Δv checked against the ship`, `decision 39: Places in scope`) needs rails behaviour `docs/architecture.md` "Rails" does not yet name. Bring the architecture in step; no game code.

- Hyperbolic rails: an object on a geocentric hyperbola (the invented passing rock: v∞ 0.5–1.0 km/s, perigee 7,378 km) propagates exactly by the hyperbolic Kepler equation; elements ↔ state in `orbits.lisp` cover e > 1.
- Rails across spheres of influence: an object on heliocentric elements outside Earth''s sphere and on geocentric elements inside it, switched at the sphere''s boundary (state → elements in the new body, as the ship''s re-centring does in `docs/architecture.md` "Frames"); precomputed once per object, so `place-state(t)` stays a pure function of t.
- Re-entry: a rails object whose orbit meets a body''s crash sphere (Derelict K-17 released at a 90 km perigee) is removed at the crossing ("burned up"), found exactly as the ship''s swept test does; drag stays out (`decision 40: Earth''s look and drag`).
- The start orbit is now polar (`decision 38: Start orbit: polar`); check the architecture''s examples and tests that name the start orbit (the 51.6° drift and J2 test orbits may stay as test cases).
- Tests in "Testing", "Rails, orbits and frames": hyperbolic propagation round trip, the SOI switch continuous in position and velocity, the removal time against the analytic perigee crossing.', '2026-10-14T18:42:31Z', '2026-10-14T19:24:18Z', 42, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (49, 10, 'Design: attitude modes, mass properties and collision shapes of every place', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md', '`docs/architecture.md` "Rails" and "Collisions and the Sun" (`task 46: Architecture: contact, berthing and life-support events in hazards and warp`, `decision 44: Contact, capture and berthing in the simulation`) make objects rigid bodies: towable objects (pods, bagged rocks, Derelict K-17) with mass, inertia tensor and a torque-free spin, berth objects (stations, depots) immovable with a kinematic attitude mode (held in the orbital frame, inertial, or Sun-pointing). `docs/design.md` "The places" gives these only for some places. Complete it; no game code.

- For each place and object of "Earth-orbit points of interest", "The Moon" (Peary Depot) and "Asteroids" (Skua Yard''s rocks, the rock mover, the passing rock): attitude mode (berth objects) or spin axis and rate (towable ones; K-17 0.3°/s about its long axis is given; rocks: state one, e.g. none or a slow tumble within the 0.5°/s capture tolerance), mass and inertia tensor about the CoM (sphere 2/5 m r², cylinder, or boxes; formula stated), collision shapes as spheres or boxes with dimensions and positions in the object''s body axes (Tern Station''s four boxes and K-17''s one box are given; Fulmar Depot, Highport, Peary Depot, the rock mover, cargo pods are not), and each fixture''s position and outward axis in those axes.
- Keep the shapes few (one to five per object), as the contact test''s cost in `docs/architecture.md` assumes.
- Check against `decision 33: Grapple tolerances, contact and berthing` (a towable fixture''s spin must allow capture) and `decision 39: Places in scope`.', '2026-10-14T18:50:52Z', '2026-10-14T19:32:14Z', 46, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (50, 11, 'create tasks for plan 11: story', 'split', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-14, tasks.sql: tasks 51-53 for plan 11', 'Split `plan 11: story` into tasks and identify all decisions that need to be made. If the plan already has tasks, its
done and dropped ones stay as they are (pm refuses to change them): drop the open ones that no longer fit and add
tasks for what the plan asks beyond them. A task that writes a plan gets `--kind plan`.', '2026-10-14T19:33:18Z', '2026-10-14T19:34:35Z', 12, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (51, 11, 'Story: setting, characters, premise, start date and names', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/story.md (Setting, Characters, Premise, Names and terms; quest line and telling left as PLACEHOLDER(52)/(53)), docs/design.md and docs/architecture.md names and date; decisions 48-50; follow-up task 54', 'First part of `plan 11: story`: create `docs/story.md` with the sections "Setting", "Characters", "Premise" and "Names and terms" (the quest line and "How the story is told" follow in the next tasks of the plan; leave their headings with a one-line `PLACEHOLDER(<task id>)`-style note naming the task that fills them).

Read first: the plan body (`pm show p11`, its "Ground rules" and "docs/story.md: contents"), `docs/design.md` (all; above all "The game in one page", "The places", "Messages and radio", "Dying and what follows", "Scope", "What the story may use"), `docs/architecture.md` (places.lisp, quests.lisp, units.lisp, "Rails"), `pm milestone show 5`, `pm decision list --answered`. Binding: the decisions listed in the plan''s ground rules (22, 24-27, 33-35, 37-39, 41, 42), `decision 14: Units and time epoch`, `decision 18: Ephemerides`.

What to write:
- Setting: the early-2040s near-Earth economy of the polar plane (Tern Station, Fulmar Depot, Highport and its water plant, Skua Yard, Peary Depot, K-17 and the debris company), who owns what, a tug pilot''s life; plausible, small, sober; no aliens, secret tech, weapons or money (`decision 26`, `decision 41`).
- Start date (`*start-date*`, default 2040-01-01 00:00 UTC, game time before 2050-01-01): choose it so the quest line''s windows work: the Moon''s best month for a TLI from Highport''s perigee (`docs/design.md` "The Moon": the Moon crossing the polar plane near RA ~90°, Dec ~+24°; compute with Meeus ch. 47 or a throwaway script, state the method and result) and the passing rock''s perigee date ("Asteroids"), allowing for the expected time the earlier quests take (rough: a few days per Earth-orbit quest, ~1 day per Highport orbit, ~5 days per lunar leg). Keep the start orbit''s phase of `decision 38: Start orbit: polar` unless the date forces a change; if the date changes the start''s lighting (sunlit, beta -10°), check and state it, and update `docs/design.md` "The start" if needed.
- Characters: the pilot (the player; no gender, no face, addressed in text only), the ship''s name and previous owner, the employer(s), every RADIO speaker (call sign, role, voice in text, location for light time), named other ships (`decision 27`: other Mule tugs, the tanker, the crew capsule, the rock mover, the bagger probe), which are scenery and which move on rails (milestone 5 "should").
- Static texts: the ship''s name above the window and up to three tape notes, exact wording (`decision 37`).
- Premise: why the pilot is here, what they want, what goes on around them, and the ending: a hook that opens the longer adventure without needing anything cut. The short introduction for `milestone 6` (a few sentences, exact text).
- Names and terms: one list of every name fixed (characters, call signs, ship, companies, places, the passing rock''s designation in Minor Planet Center style, matching the chosen date''s year).
- Renamings: if a place is renamed, update `docs/design.md` and `docs/architecture.md` in the same change (grep every occurrence).
- `*start-date*` in `docs/architecture.md` / `docs/design.md`: update wherever the default date is named, if it changes. If `src/units.lisp` already holds the date constant, add a follow-up task in the milestone 5 masterplan context instead of changing code (`milestone 5` sets the story''s date); note it.

Decisions to record (`pm decision record`): setting and premise (the pilot''s situation, the employer, where the prelude ends); names (ship, characters and call signs, companies, places kept or renamed, the passing rock''s designation); the start date (and the start orbit''s phase if changed). Add `pm decision consequences` to `decision 39: Places in scope` if places are renamed, and to `decision 14` for the date.

Done when: the four sections exist in `docs/story.md` per `AGENTS.md` style (intro paragraph per top-level heading, concise bullets); the date''s windows are computed and stated; design.md and architecture.md agree with every name and the date; the decisions are recorded.', '2026-10-14T19:34:24Z', '2026-10-14T19:42:13Z', 50, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (52, 11, 'Story: the quest line, its steps, completion conditions and checks', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/story.md', 'Second part of `plan 11: story`: write "The quest line" in `docs/story.md`, on top of the setting, characters, names and start date written by `task 51: Story: setting, characters, premise, start date and names` (read its decisions: `pm decision list --answered --grep story --grep name --grep date`).

Read first: the plan body (`pm show p11`, "The quest line" and "Ground rules"), `docs/design.md` ("Δv for the standard legs", "The places", "Δv checked against the ship", "The autopilot", "Grappling and berthing", "Towing", "Dying and what follows", "Saving", "Scope", "What the story may use"), `docs/architecture.md` ("Scripted runs", "Rails", "Re-entry of objects", quests.lisp, saves.lisp), `decision 33: Grapple tolerances, contact and berthing`, `decision 34: How death works`, `decision 35: Saving and audio`, `decision 42: Scope: what each milestone builds`.

What to write:
- 5 to 10 quests in a fixed order, as a table (number, title, giver, place(s), skills, milestone 2-5, Δv, time) and then one subsection per quest.
- The arc the plan asks for: manual attitude and a small burn in the start orbit; rendezvous, grapple, berthing and refuelling (Tern Station, Fulmar Depot); the derelict K-17 pushed to re-entry by hand (`docs/design.md` "The derelict''s re-entry"; the autopilot refuses below 150 km); the trip to Highport; towing a Skua Yard rock (20-100 t; the 150 t one refused); a lunar transfer to Peary Depot; the passing rock if built (milestone 4 "should"); a close call with the Sun''s warning zone only if it fits Δv and 180 person-days (`docs/design.md`: LEO → 0.551 AU 4,143 m/s, by hand only), otherwise the Sun stays a danger told about.
- Per quest: title, giver (RADIO sender), goal, place(s), skills taught (controls, holds, presets, instruments by their `docs/design.md` names), the milestone that makes it playable, propellant and time needed from the expected state at its start (Δv from `docs/design.md` tables, cited; a leg not listed gets its formula and result), steps (each a JOB card title plus up to three lines, which need Y), the triggers of its RADIO messages (exact texts may be drafted here; the next task finalises them), the completion condition per step, its checkpoints.
- Completion conditions machine-checkable from simulation state only (berthed at a fixture, grappled object id, orbit elements within tolerances, an object removed with its cause, a body''s sphere entered, time elapsed, Y acknowledged); name the state each reads per `docs/architecture.md`; tolerances in numbers.
- Running checks: propellant and person-days carried from quest to quest (refuelling only berthed at Fulmar Depot, Highport, Peary Depot; restock at Tern Station, Highport, Peary Depot), each within 6.65 km/s empty, 1.74 km/s with 50 t, 1.02 km/s with 100 t, and 180 person-days.
- Failure and recovery: death never fails a quest, the step is flown again from the last checkpoint (`decision 34`); a step that can be made impossible (rock pushed away, propellant spent far from a depot, K-17 pushed wrong) says how the game recovers without new mechanics (objects reset from the checkpoint, a tanker or the employer''s offer by RADIO).
- Quests built on a "should" (the passing rock, story ships moving on rails) say so and what the line does if it is dropped (skipped or replaced; the line stays complete).
- Nothing cut or not yet built at the quest''s milestone; no weapons, landing, money, EVA, docking ports, reply choices.

Decision to record (`pm decision record`): the quest line: its quests in order, each with its milestone, and what happens if a "should" it relies on is dropped.

Follow-ups: a Δv leg, place detail, fixture or flight script (`flights/<name>.sexp`, `decision 21: Physics test bounds and flight scripts`) that `milestone 5`''s headless play-through needs and the design lacks: `pm task add` in the plan it belongs to (design gaps to `plan 10: game design` while it has open tasks, else as a note for the milestone''s masterplan via a task in this plan).

Done when: "The quest line" has 5-10 quests each with every per-quest item above, every Δv and duration checked with citations, the decision recorded.', '2026-10-14T19:34:24Z', '2026-10-14T20:01:30Z', 50, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (53, 11, 'Story: how it is told, every RADIO and JOB text, read-through', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/story.md (''How the story is told''; every RADIO as per-quest tables with ids, triggers, Y and exact text, the D table and S1; quest 8''s cards; cards fixed to the autopilot chains; tape notes'' line breaks; introduction corrected; THRIFT and TANKER 3 schedules), docs/design.md (Skua Yard spacing, story ships'' trips, S1, pointer from ''Messages and radio''); decision 57; follow-up task 58. scripts/test could not run in this session: libSDL3.so not found (environment; docs-only change).', 'Third part of `plan 11: story`: write "How the story is told" in `docs/story.md` and fix every text the game shows, then read the whole document against `docs/design.md`. Builds on `task 51: Story: setting, characters, premise, start date and names` and `task 52: Story: the quest line, its steps, completion conditions and checks`.

Read first: `docs/story.md` as written, `docs/design.md` "Messages and radio", "The cockpit" (COMMS screen, dot-matrix, MSG lamp, readability at 1280 × 800), "Scope", "What the story may use", `decision 37: Message channels the story may use`, `decision 27: Other ships`.

What to write:
- "How the story is told": which channel carries what (RADIO, JOB, SHIP stays the game''s, static texts); the radio''s tone (terse working people, numbers as pilots say them); what COMMS shows between quests; how light time shows at the Moon (1.3 s each way, the sender''s position); what the player sees of other ships at work (scenery at places, departures and arrivals on rails out of view, milestone 5 "should").
- Every RADIO message of every quest in exact text, with sender call sign and trigger; every JOB card in exact text (title, up to three lines; fit the COMMS width of `docs/design.md` "The cockpit"); which need Y. Keep them in the quest subsections or one table per quest, so `quests.lisp` can copy them.
- Exact wording of the tape notes and the ship''s name (if the first task left drafts), and the `milestone 6` introduction (check it reads as the README''s short intro too).
- Read-through: every feature a quest uses is assigned to milestones 2-5 in `docs/design.md` "Feature list" at or before the quest''s milestone; no cut feature; names match "Names and terms", `docs/design.md` and `docs/architecture.md`; the intro paragraph per top-level heading and bullet style per `AGENTS.md`; no placeholder notes left from the earlier tasks. Fix what disagrees, in the document that is wrong; a disagreement that needs a design change goes as `pm task add` to the plan it belongs to.

Done when: `docs/story.md` is complete per the plan''s "Done when" (sections, 5-10 quests with all items, every message and card in exact text), and agrees with `docs/design.md` and `docs/architecture.md`.', '2026-10-14T19:34:24Z', '2026-10-14T21:03:49Z', 50, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (54, 10, 'Design: the story''s extra ships (THRIFT, TANKER 3, BAGGER 3) in docs/design.md', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/story.md, docs/architecture.md; decision 51: Story ships flying free: THRIFT, TANKER 3, BAGGER 3', '`task 51: Story: setting, characters, premise, start date and names` named the other ships in `docs/story.md` "Characters", "Other ships" (`decision 49: Story: names, call signs and ships`). Three of them are objects that `docs/design.md` does not yet define:
- THRIFT (Mule M-09) and TANKER 3 (uncrewed tanker): between trips in Highport''s orbit, 5 km and 2 km behind Highport; they move on rails (Highport ↔ Peary Depot, Highport ↔ Fulmar Depot) as `milestone 5`''s "should" ("Story ships moving between places", `decision 27: Other ships`); if that is dropped they are not drawn.
- BAGGER 3: the uncrewed bagger probe that nets 2040 BQ7 and rides 1 km ahead of it on its rails until the pilot grapples the rock (`docs/design.md` "Asteroids" calls it scenery on rails); the story sketches it as a 1.5 m box with two small solar wings.

What to do in `docs/design.md`:
- "Other ships": add the bagger probe as a kind (built from, dimensions, job).
- "The places", "Rigid bodies: attitude, mass, shapes and fixtures": a row each for a free-flying Mule (THRIFT; the Mule''s own shapes, no fixture usable by the player or a berth-like immovable object, as the rock mover), a free-flying tanker and the bagger probe: kind, attitude mode, mass, shapes, bound; and where they sit in Highport''s orbit (M₀ offsets as Skua Yard''s).
- Check that 5 km and 2 km behind Highport stay clear of the approach to Highport''s free fixture and of Skua Yard (30 km behind); move them if not, and update `docs/story.md` in step.
Done when: the three objects are defined like the other places'' objects and `docs/story.md` agrees.', '2026-10-14T19:42:10Z', '2026-10-14T19:47:59Z', 51, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (55, 10, 'Design: deliveries, the stranded offer, checkpoint floors and POD 14 for the quest line', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/story.md; decision 53', '`docs/story.md` "The quest line" (`task 52: Story: the quest line, its steps, completion conditions and checks`) relies on four things `docs/design.md` and `docs/architecture.md` do not yet say. Add them, citing the story''s "Rules for every quest" where it defines them, and keep its numbers.

- **Deliveries**: a load released with its CoM within 100 m of a receiving fixture''s pin (Highport''s plant fixture; Peary Depot''s berth) and at most 0.05 m/s relative to the receiving object, still within 150 m 600 s later, is taken in by the place''s handling gear: removed from the simulation with cause `:delivered`, reusing the removal of `docs/architecture.md` "Re-entry of objects" (removed objects keep their id, time, body, cause). Write it into `docs/design.md` "Grappling and berthing" or "Towing" and `docs/architecture.md` "Re-entry of objects" (generalise to "Removal of objects"), with a test line in "Testing" (`tests/hazards.lisp` or `tests/quests.lisp`).
- **The stranded offer**: when the ship (outside a berth) has less Δv with its load than the current quest step''s floor, is outbound on an escape path (e ≥ 1 around Earth past perigee, or the Sun dominant), or the step''s object can no longer be reached, CAIRN OPS sends a RADIO after 10 min game time; Y restores the last checkpoint exactly as the LOST panel''s Return. Add to `docs/design.md` "Dying and what follows" (it already says "the story''s employer can send a tanker as a quest may decide").
- **Checkpoint floors**: a quest step has a Δv floor (m/s, with the load it carries or will carry); checkpoints (step start, berthing, completed plan) are not written while the ship''s Δv remaining is below it. Add to `docs/design.md` "Saving" and `docs/architecture.md` "Checkpoints".
- **POD 14**: a standard 12 t cargo pod (`docs/design.md` "Rigid bodies", "Cargo pod (standard)") parked in Skua Yard for quest 7; give its elements (Highport''s orbit, a mean anomaly among the rocks, clear of the approach to Highport and of the rocks'' 300–800 m spacing), attitude (inertial, no spin) and list it in "Earth-orbit points of interest" and the rigid-bodies table; add it to `docs/story.md` "Names and terms" if missing.

Done when the four are in the docs, consistent with `docs/story.md`, and `decision 39: Places in scope` gets a consequence note for POD 14.', '2026-10-14T20:00:44Z', '2026-10-14T20:06:42Z', 52, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (56, 10, 'Design: autopilot rendezvous for the quest line: phasing, Peary Depot''s plane, a hyperbolic target', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md (''Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach''; ''The autopilot'', ''The Moon'', ''Asteroids'', ''Δv checked against the ship'', scope rows), docs/story.md (quests 7 and 9 figures, running checks, 9.5 drop point); decisions 54, 55 (partly supersedes 50); task 57 body extended with start states for the rendezvous scripts', '`docs/story.md` "The quest line" (`task 52: Story: the quest line, its steps, completion conditions and checks`) budgets ≤ 50 m/s of phasing per rendezvous and uses presets `docs/design.md` "The autopilot" does not fully define. Extend "The autopilot" (and `decision 32: Autopilot scope and safety rules` by a recorded decision if the rule changes):

- **Phasing for co-altitude targets**: the rendezvous'' Lambert search (departures over 48 h, transfers of 0.4–1.5 periods) cannot cheaply close a large phase gap between orbits of equal or near-equal period (Fulmar Depot after the K-17 job, Peary Depot after LOI, Highport after a lunar return, Skua Yard after the BQ7 capture). Add multi-revolution phasing orbits (e.g. a phasing ellipse held for N revolutions) so the cost stays ≤ ~50 m/s within a stated time; state the search and its bounds.
- **Peary Depot from Earth orbit**: the TLI preset targets a lunar periapsis altitude and inclination only; aim it at Peary Depot''s plane (i 90°, Ω 0° against the Moon''s equator) and arrival phase, or offer "Rendezvous: Peary Depot" as a chain TLI → LOI → rendezvous. Check the Δv against "The Moon" (1,193 m/s from Highport''s perigee in the best window, 12 t pod aboard in quest 7).
- **A target on a hyperbola** ("Rendezvous: 2040 BQ7"): "0.4–1.5 periods" has no meaning for a hyperbola; define transfer times (e.g. 3–8 days from Highport''s perigee) and the departure search, aiming 1 km behind the rock on its fixture axis (`docs/design.md` "Asteroids"), with the story''s dates (`decision 50`: perigee 2040-03-12 12:00 UTC, departure ~2040-03-05, latest 2040-03-06).
- Each with a headless test line in `milestone 3` / `milestone 4` terms ("Scripted runs").
- **Approach inside Skua Yard** (found by `task 55: Design: deliveries, the stranded offer, checkpoint floors and POD 14 for the quest line`): the yard is a string along Highport''s orbit, objects 666.7 m apart at apogee (`docs/design.md` "Earth-orbit points of interest", "Layout"), so the aim point 1 km behind a target lies mid-gap, 333 m from both neighbours, but a straight terminal path from it to the target''s fixture axis passes the neighbour 667 m behind the target. Define a terminal path that clears it (e.g. an offset approach out of the orbit''s line, or a radial/R-bar approach in the yard), with a clearance stated against the objects'' bounds.', '2026-10-14T20:00:44Z', '2026-10-14T20:37:19Z', 52, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (57, 10, 'Architecture: flight-script actions for the quest play-through', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/architecture.md (Scripted runs, Files in load order), docs/design.md, docs/story.md; decision 56', '`milestone 5: Story and quests: the playable prelude` must play the whole quest line headless (`docs/story.md` "The quest line", `task 52: Story: the quest line, its steps, completion conditions and checks`). The flight-script vocabulary of `docs/architecture.md` "Scripted runs" (`decision 21: Physics test bounds and flight scripts`) has burns, holds, waits and `(:autopilot …)`, but not what the quests need. Extend "Scripted runs":

- Actions: `(:target <id>)`, `(:grapple :arm)`, `(:release)`, `(:transfer :on)`, `(:ack)` (Y), `(:approach <fixture> :speed 0.1)` – a closed-loop terminal approach from the autopilot''s 100 m station to capture, writing `controls` like a pilot (target hold, fine RCS translation), not a shortcut; `(:wait :quest-step <n.m>)`, `(:wait :date "2040-01-21")`, `(:expect :quest-step <n.m>)`.
- The manual parts: quest 1''s turns and burns, quest 3''s push below 150 km by hand (hold retrograde, throttle, cut at a periapsis), as scripted holds and `:after-dv` / `(:wait :periapsis-below …)` cuts.
- One script per quest, `flights/quest-1.sexp` … `flights/quest-9.sexp`, each starting from the previous one''s end state (a save), and a test that chains them to the ending; state its expected run time at warp.
- Start states for scripts that do not begin at the start date: `docs/design.md` "Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach", "Scripted runs" (`task 56: Design: autopilot rendezvous for the quest line: phasing, Peary Depot''s plane, a hyperbolic target`) lists six rendezvous scripts that start from a stated state (a date, an orbit or a place''s slot, tanks, a grappled load); give "Scripted runs" the action that sets it (e.g. `(:start <checkpoint file or state>)`) and list those scripts with their `:expect`s.
Done when "Scripted runs" lists the actions and the scripts, and `milestone 5`''s play-through can be written from it.', '2026-10-14T20:00:44Z', '2026-10-14T20:52:32Z', 52, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (58, 11, 'Design: parking slots and moves of the story ships THRIFT and TANKER 3', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md (''Earth-orbit points of interest'': TANKER 3''s Fulmar slot and clearances; ''The Moon'': THRIFT''s Peary slot and the LOI check; plan check in ''The terminal path and crowded targets''; Rigid bodies, feature list), docs/architecture.md (''Story ships'' schedules'', checkpoints, test), docs/story.md (TANKER 3 leaves Fulmar 2040-03-06 06:00); decision 58; follow-up task 59', 'Follow-up of `task 53: Story: how it is told, every RADIO and JOB text, read-through` and `decision 57: Story: how it is told, its texts and the story ships'' schedule` (in this plan since `plan 10: game design` is closed).

`docs/story.md` "Other ships" and "Other ships at their work" now schedule the moving story ships (`milestone 5` "should"): THRIFT leaves its slot ahead of Highport on 2040-01-21 06:00 and parks in Peary Depot''s orbit half a turn ahead of the depot from 2040-01-26 06:00; TANKER 3 leaves on 2040-01-21 06:00, parks 2 km ahead of Fulmar Depot in its orbit from 2040-01-22 06:00, and is back in its slot ahead of Highport from 2040-03-07 06:00. A move leaves one slot and appears in the next, not drawn in transit; each switch waits while the player''s ship is within 200 km of the slot (`decision 27: Other ships`).

Do:
- `docs/design.md` "Earth-orbit points of interest" and "The Moon": the elements of the two new slots (THRIFT in Peary Depot''s orbit, u0 + 180 deg; TANKER 3 on Fulmar Depot''s elements, 2 km ahead), checked for clearance against the autopilot''s aim points and terminal paths ("Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach": >= 200 m beyond every other object''s bound) at Fulmar Depot (fixture A''s approach) and Peary Depot (the LOI phasing orbit and the approach); attitude as their Highport slots ("Rigid bodies").
- `docs/architecture.md` "Rails" (or a new subsection): a story ship''s schedule as a list of (slot elements, from-time) with a transit gap; place-state(t) nil in transit; the 200 km deferral as a deterministic rule evaluated on the step grid, kept in the simulation state (checkpoints, saves); the quest messages D2, D3 and 7f triggered by the actual switch; a test (deferral while within 200 km, switch at the first step beyond).
- Keep `docs/story.md` in step if a time or slot changes; record a decision if the schedule changes.', '2026-10-14T21:03:29Z', '2026-10-14T21:10:34Z', 53, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (59, 11, 'Design: rendezvous transfers from below pass the target before the aim point', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/story.md; decision 59', 'Follow-up of `task 58: Design: parking slots and moves of the story ships THRIFT and TANKER 3` (in `plan 11: story` since `plan 10: game design` is closed).

Found while checking TANKER 3''s Fulmar slot: `docs/design.md` "Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach" aims 1 km behind the target and holds only the terminal path and the aim point to the clearance rule (`decision 54: Autopilot rendezvous: phasing, lunar chain, hyperbolic targets, clear approaches`). A Hohmann-like transfer from a lower orbit arrives at its apoapsis slower than the target, so in Clohessy–Wiltshire terms it overshoots ahead of the aim point by ~0.12 × the height difference and falls back along the orbit: from a 370 km drift orbit to Fulmar Depot (quest 4) it overshoots 15.5 km and passes the depot''s CoM ~30 m away (100 km below: ~40 m; 30 km below: ~130 m), before the braking burn. Linear model, impulsive; a throwaway check, not committed.

Do:
- Check the cases with the shooting''s figures (or a Lambert script): Tern Station from the start (quest 2), Fulmar Depot from 370/400 km (quest 4), K-17 from 400 km, Highport from Fulmar (quest 5, arrival at apogee from below).
- Fix in `docs/design.md` "The terminal path and crowded targets": e.g. extend the plan check (`decision 58: Story ships'' slots at Fulmar Depot and Peary Depot, schedules and clear plans`, now for objects other than the target) to the target itself (>= 200 m beyond its bound until the aim point), or prefer transfer times that arrive from behind/below; give the Δv cost against the quest tables ("The quest line''s rendezvous", `docs/story.md` running checks) and update them if it changes.
- `docs/architecture.md` "Scripts by milestone": a `:clearance-above` expectation on `rendezvous-fulmar-phasing` covering the target until the aim point.
- Record a decision refining `decision 54`.', '2026-10-14T21:10:30Z', '2026-10-14T21:16:42Z', 58, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (60, 12, 'create tasks for plan 12: consistency check and sign-off', 'split', 'done', 1000, '2026-10-14, tasks.sql: tasks 61-67 for plan 12; no decisions needed', 'Split `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off` into tasks and identify all decisions that need to be made. If the plan already has tasks, its
done and dropped ones stay as they are (pm refuses to change them): drop the open ones that no longer fit and add
tasks for what the plan asks beyond them. A task that writes a plan gets `--kind plan`.', '2026-10-14T21:18:28Z', '2026-10-14T21:19:48Z', 13, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (61, 12, 'Check figures, dates and names across the documents', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/story.md, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. Checked: ship figures (28 t, v_e 4,410, 6,650/1,738/1,017 m/s, 180 person-days, 10 kg/s) in all docs; every quest''s Δv and propellant recomputed by the rocket equation (dry 7,961 kg) against design ''Δv for the standard legs'', ''Earth-orbit points of interest'', ''The Moon'', ''Δv checked against the ship'', ''Rendezvous'' and decision 55, plus story ''Running checks'' and the flight scripts'' :dv-below and :propellant-above; dates (start, TLI 01-20 06:01, Moon 01-26 02:36, BQ7 found 01-19, meeting 03-10 ~23:00, perigee 03-12 12:00, TANKER 3 schedule) against decisions 50, 55, 58; names, call signs and ids of story ''Names and terms'' in design and architecture; units, frames, epoch and constants of decision 14. Quest 7''s ''1,378 + 1,353'' was right (25 to POD 14 + 1,353 out, then 1,353 back; 12,821 kg out = 203 + 12,618) but unclear. Changed: story quest table row 7 Δv and stores cells (≤ 12 days away out, as its Propellant line and Running checks say, not ≤ 7 per leg); story quest 4 gain on Fulmar 7.8°/orbit, 2.96 days (as design); story Running checks TLI at 2040-01-20 06:01 (decision 55); architecture quest-3 :propellant-above 22310 (Running checks'' 22,870 less 560; was 22,333, stale); design Highport TLI 376 m/s from the 2040-01-20 06:01 perigee (was 370 and ''near 01-21'', decision 55); design TANKER 3 Fulmar slot r = 6,878.1366 km (R⊕ of decision 14); design BQ7 check ''stack (58 t dry, 72.6 t wet)''; design rigid-body rows named GRINDSTONE and 2040 BQ7.', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

## What to check
- The ship''s figures in every document match `docs/design.md` "Parts", "Mass budget and Δv": 28 t of LH2/LOX, v_e 4,410 m/s, 6,650 m/s empty, 1,738 m/s with 50 t, 1,017 m/s with 100 t, 180 person-days, 10 kg/s transfer.
- Δv per leg in `docs/story.md` (quest table, per-quest "Propellant" lines, "Running checks") against `docs/design.md` "Δv for the standard legs", "Earth-orbit points of interest", "The Moon", "Δv checked against the ship", "Rendezvous: search, phasing and the approach" and `decision 55: Meeting 2040 BQ7 and the lunar arrival from the polar plane`.
  - Known suspect: quest 7''s "1,378 + 1,353" in the quest table, while `docs/design.md` gives 1,273 m/s for Highport → Peary Depot (1,353 with margin). Recompute or correct it, and the "Running checks" propellant and the flight scripts'' `:dv-below` and `:propellant-above` in `docs/architecture.md` that follow from it.
- Dates and times: start 2040-01-01 00:00 UTC, TLI 2040-01-20 06:01, Moon at Highport''s apogee 2040-01-26 02:36, BQ7 found 2040-01-19, meeting ~2040-03-10 23:00, perigee 2040-03-12 12:00, TANKER 3 leaving Fulmar 2040-03-06 06:00. The same in story, design, the architecture''s flight scripts and `decision 50`, `decision 55`, `decision 58` (`pm show d50` etc. for their subjects).
- Names and ids: place names, call signs, ship names and the ids of `docs/story.md` "Names and terms" ("Proposed ids") used identically in `docs/design.md` (places, fixtures, rigid bodies) and `docs/architecture.md` (flight scripts, start states, removal causes `:burned-up`, `:delivered`).
- Units, frames and epoch: SI and `double-float` world positions, frames (heliocentric, planet-centred, ship-local FRD), the epoch and constants of `decision 14: Units and time epoch`; the same wherever the documents give formulas or figures.

## Done when
