INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (63, 12, 'Check luv capabilities, wishlist and architecture against each other', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md. Checked: each of the 12 gaps in luv-capabilities ''Gaps and workarounds'' plus ''Other findings'' against architecture ''Written here'' and ''Files in load order'' (all had a workaround, none named its file) and against the wishlist (every reusable gap has a line; starfield and instancing are game-specific); every wishlist line against a finding (two rested on none: the recipe deleting all but fonts/ at ../luv/flake.nix:720, and the Objective-C bridge writing ../build/*.dylib; both verified in ../luv and added); the architecture''s luv reliances: reversed-Z, camera-relative single floats, sdl3-image (ran, runs 29-33), dot-matrix overlay and report-failed-live-artifacts (built here, src/scene.lisp, src/main.lisp), Slug text and render-to-texture-then-sample (ran via Luvcraft''s smoke test, run 28), audio-sink (only read: now ran, run 35 on SDL''s dummy driver; a failing driver signals an error), no Ghostty per decision 36 everywhere; budgets: clock 4 ms / 4,096 steps, prediction 1 ms, rest 6 ms, x100,000 ~830 steps, x1,000,000 ~x490,000, play-through ~15 s, test budgets: arithmetic consistent with ~180 ns per step. Changed: luv-capabilities adds the CPU, run 28''s render-to-texture finding, the two packaging/platform findings, ''luv''s developer'' for the M2 Pro line, the integrator measurement and the budgets resting on it in ''Performance'' (GPU side not measured, iGPU target), audio sink ran with run 35; wishlist cites Platforms for the bridge and says the terminal-wall line has no workaround here (cut by decision 36); architecture ''Written here'' names each workaround''s file and adds the ''Other findings'' items, audio-sink cites run 35