INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (64, 12, 'Check that every feature is assigned and the milestones agree with the scope', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. Checked: every feature named in design.md''s Ship, Flight, Cockpit and Places sections against ''Feature list''; architecture ''Files in load order'' milestones per file against the rows; ''Scripts by milestone'' against the Done when rows; pm milestone show 2-6 Outcome and Done when against the must rows. Changed: decision 62: Scope: must rows for each milestone''s Outcome (partly supersedes decision 42 and decision 32): scenery ships must in 3 (milestone 5''s ''other ships at their work''), real asteroids on the map must in 4 (milestone 4''s belt), the autopilot''s transfers to asteroids and planets cut (no such destination; mid-course corrections kept); new design section ''Title screen and menus'' for the milestone 6 rows that had none; rows added or extended: overlay message line and autopilot panel (3), Moon crash (2), planets'' crash spheres (4), the Moon''s orbit and map focus (4), in-game runs with screenshots per milestone 3/4/5 Done when, name plate with the cockpit (3) and registration on the hull (2); the stale row ''story''s start date, ship name and place names'' (5) removed (they arrive in 2 and 3); ''Each milestone against…'' updated. architecture.md: file milestones for autopilot, places, impostors, meshes (3: places and ships), ribbons, overlay, cockpit, camera, input (gamepad 6 could), audio (6 should). Follow-up: task 69: Architecture: the Sun-death flight script of milestone 4 (the must row has no script in ''Scripts by milestone''). No human decision needed.', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

