INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (65, 12, 'Check that the story uses only what is in scope by milestone 5', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/story.md, docs/design.md, docs/architecture.md. Checked: every place, object, skill, instrument, channel and action of quests 1-9 against the ''Scope'' feature list by milestone (2-4 for flyability, 5 for quests, RADIO, JOB); no cut feature appears (weapons, landing, EVA, docking, money, save slots, Ghostty, voices; 3a''s ''paid'' is talk, not a price). Throwaway script (/tmp, deleted): 43 JOB cards, every line <= 26 and title + step id <= 26, <= 3 lines; 58 RADIO messages (incl. D1-D7, S1), ids unique, senders all call signs of ''Names and terms'', triggers name existing steps or dates, <= 160 chars except 9h (177, the documented exception), Y flags match ''Y to copy/when ready'' and the Y steps 1.1, 2.3, 4.2, 9.2 each have their Y message and an (:ack) in their script; all 36 steps the play-through references exist. Play-through: actions, waits and start states all defined in ''Scripted runs''; each script''s end state matches the next quest''s ''Expected state at start''. Fixed: (1) POD 14 was milestone 5 although milestone 3''s Skua Yard scripts and milestone 4''s rendezvous-peary/return-highport use it: decision 63: POD 14 and Skua Yard''s layout from milestone 3 (partly supersedes decision 39), feature-list row moved to 3, design ''Earth-orbit points of interest'', ''Rigid bodies'', ''What the story may use'', architecture places.lisp; (2) 7.5 lacked the refuel at Highport that quest 8''s start state and ''Running checks'' assume: completion + ''and propellant full'', card line ''Plant fixture, then B'', quest-7 script adds (:transfer :on) and ends full; (3) 5.1''s card said two burns, 5a three: card ''Three burns''; (4) ''If a should is dropped'': without the rock quest 8 is never skipped (no 8f, 9g) and quest-8.sexp ends at wait 9.7; without moving ships D2, D3, 7f use scheduled times and the scripts are unchanged; (5) design ''Messages and radio'' SHIP now names the removal messages the story relies on; (6) architecture ''Steps'' defines a bare (:after 300).', 'Follow the "Ground rules for every task" of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: fix small, already-decided mismatches in the documents yourself and cite the decision or section; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision with `pm decision record` and updates every document citing it; a gap too large becomes a follow-up task in plan 12; work only a later milestone can do goes into `docs/design.md` "Scope"; no game features. End with a short list of what you checked and what you changed in the done note.

