INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (67, 12, 'Sign off milestone 1', 'work', 'done', 390, '2026-10-14, docs/design.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md. Checked: milestone 1 Done when against the notes of task 61 to task 66, task 68 and task 69 (figures, dates, names; decision log; capabilities, wishlist and architecture; every feature assigned, milestones 2-6 covered by must rows, no human decision; story within scope by milestone 5; clean-checkout run of every AGENTS.md command); scripts/test on the current tree: 23 passed, 0 failed; the four documents and docs/luv-wishlist.md each have an intro paragraph at the top and under each top-level heading, bullets elsewhere (one-sentence lead-ins under subsections left as they are); AGENTS.md left as the developer wrote it (the intro paragraph is allowed, not required); no TODO, TBD or FIXME; every task cited in the docs is done; PLACEHOLDER(23) and its replacement by render.lisp are in docs/architecture.md; the Scope feature list leaves nothing missing for the masterplans of milestones 2 to 6. Changed: design ''Inertia'' no longer says task 45 ''is adjusting'' the architecture (done; the architecture says the full tensor); luv-capabilities ''Starfield'' HYG ShareAlike points to architecture ''Assets'' instead of ''to be confirmed''. No follow-ups. Milestone 1 is ready for the developer''s reading; closing it is the developer''s.', 'Last task of `plan 12: consistency check and sign-off`: runs after every other task of this plan and their follow-ups.

## What to do
- Walk the Done when of `milestone 1: Scope and design: what luv can carry, what the game is` (`pm milestone show 1`):
  - The four documents (`docs/luv-capabilities.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/story.md`) exist and agree with each other: read the done notes of this plan''s check tasks (`pm show p12`).
  - The `docs/design.md` "Scope" feature list assigns every feature to milestone 2 to 6 or cuts it.
  - The skeleton builds and runs from a clean checkout (the clean-checkout task''s note) and its test passes: run `scripts/test` once more on the current tree.
- Style pass over all docs and `AGENTS.md`: an intro paragraph at the top and under each top-level heading, concise bullets elsewhere (`AGENTS.md` "Rules"); no stale text ("TODO", "TBD", references to tasks as still open that are done: check with `pm show <id>`).
- What later milestones need from the documents and is still missing: a follow-up task in this plan if the documents must say it, or a row or note in `docs/design.md` "Scope" for that milestone''s masterplan.
- Fix small things yourself; a fix that changes a lasting choice supersedes its decision (`pm decision record`).

## Done when
- Nothing is left; the done note says briefly what was checked and that `milestone 1` is ready for the developer''s reading. Closing the milestone is the developer''s, not this task''s.', '2026-10-14T21:19:46Z', '2026-10-14T21:54:43Z', 60, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (68, 12, 'scripts/test fails when started from an inherited luv dev-shell environment', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, scripts/test, scripts/screenshot, sly, flake.nix, AGENTS.md, docs/architecture.md. Cause: the inherited LD_LIBRARY_PATH starts with a host alsa-lib built against glibc 2.43; libSDL3.so pulls libasound from it and fails against luv''s glibc 2.42 (the same flake, not a stale cache). Fix: the three scripts always re-enter nix develop (~0.6 s; its hook unsets LD_LIBRARY_PATH) unless LIS_DEV_SHELL=1, set by their re-exec and by the flake check; decision 64: Scripts always re-enter the dev shell. Checked in the inherited env: scripts/test 23 passed (~5 s), scripts/screenshot, ./sly start/eval/status/stop; nix flake check passed (~16 s). AGENTS.md Commands notes the pitfall.', 'Found by `task 63: Check luv capabilities, wishlist and architecture against each other` (2026-10-14).

## Symptom
- An agent session whose environment already holds a luv dev shell (direnv: `LUV_DEV_SHELL=default`, `LUV_ASDF_CACHE_KEY=izn0rp7…-luv-development-closure`, an `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` with alsa-lib, sdl3, ffmpeg, …) ran `scripts/test`: exit 1, `CFFI:LOAD-FOREIGN-LIBRARY-ERROR` "Unable to load any of the alternatives: ("libSDL3.so" …)" while loading cl-sdl3''s `lib.fasl`; the same with `env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH`.
- `env -u LUV_DEV_SHELL -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH scripts/test` passed (23 passed, 0 failed): `scripts/test` skips `nix develop` when `LUV_DEV_SHELL` is set and then runs in the inherited, possibly stale, environment.
- `scripts/screenshot` uses the same guard; `./sly` likely too.

## What to do
- Find the cause (stale direnv cache vs. the current flake, the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` that the shell hook normally unsets, the native environment activation).
- Make the scripts robust: e.g. re-enter `nix develop` unless the inherited shell is this flake''s current one, or unset `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and re-run `luv_activate_native_environment`; keep `nix flake check` working.
- Note the pitfall in `AGENTS.md` "Commands" if a rule for agents remains (e.g. `direnv reload`).', '2026-10-14T21:28:37Z', '2026-10-14T21:42:49Z', 63, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (69, 12, 'Architecture: the Sun-death flight script of milestone 4', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md, docs/story.md. Checked by a throwaway two-body script (finite burns in Earth''s field, patched at Earth''s sphere, hull rule on the heliocentric ellipse): the polar plane allows the dive only near an equinox (on 2040-01-01 Earth''s velocity is 80 deg out of it); one full-tank burn from 400 km reaches only 0.329 AU (pilot lives), two burns (2,000 m/s, then 4,600 centred on perigee) reach 0.317 AU with ~90 kg left; from Highport''s perigee the least perihelion is 0.67 AU; 2040-03-24 keeps the escape 288,000 km from the Moon (03-20: 8,200 km). Changed: architecture ''Scripts by milestone'' milestone 4 gains sun-dive (row, written-out script, why, timeline 2040-03-24 to death 2040-06-25 at 0.3255 AU, ~5,000 steps, < 1 s); ''Waits and expectations'' gains :sun-distance-below/above, :hull-above/below, :drop-out <kind> and the :lost causes; design ''The Sun'' and ''Δv checked against the ship'' corrected (equinox, two burns, Highport not a start), feature-list row names sun-dive; story ''Not a quest'' drops the Highport figure. Cites decision 34: How death works and decision 56: Flight-script actions, start states and the quest play-through; no lasting choice changed, no decision recorded. scripts/test passes.', 'Found by `task 64: Check that every feature is assigned and the milestones agree with the scope`. `docs/design.md` "Feature list" has the must row "Sun death flight script" (milestone 4; `milestone 4`''s Done when: "Flying towards the Sun kills the pilot, tested"), and "The Sun" says the test is "a flight script with that burn" (a dive from Earth orbit, 6,360 m/s from LEO on full tanks to the deadly 0.326 AU, or 3,758 m/s from Highport''s perigee). `docs/architecture.md` "Scripts by milestone" lists no such script for `milestone 4` (only `rendezvous-peary`, `return-highport`, `intercept-bq7`); only unit tests of the hull rule exist ("Rails, orbits and frames" / "Warp, events and collisions").

## Do
- Compute a flyable dive (throwaway script, not committed): which start state (`docs/architecture.md` "Start states": a date, `:orbit` in the polar plane or `(:elements …)`) and which burn put the ship on a heliocentric path to a perihelion ≤ 0.326 AU within one tank. Check that the polar plane (i 90°, Ω 270°) allows the departure asymptote against Earth''s heliocentric velocity at the chosen date (near an equinox the ecliptic''s velocity direction lies close to the y–z plane), or else start from stated heliocentric or departure elements and say why; correct the figures in `docs/design.md` "The Sun" and "Δv checked against the ship" if they change.
- Add the script (e.g. `sun-dive`) to `docs/architecture.md` "Scripts by milestone", `milestone 4`, in the table''s terms: start state, actions (holds, throttle, `:after-dv`, `(:warp :coast)`), and expectations: the warp drop-out on entering 0.551 AU, the danger mark, death by heat with `(:expect :lost :heat)`. If a wait or condition is missing (e.g. a wait on the hull temperature or on the dominant body being the Sun), add it to "Waits and expectations" with its milestone.
- Keep the expected run time small (state the steps at coarse warp over ~100 days) and note it.
