- Contents: the `body` struct and a fixed list `:sun`, `:earth`, `:moon` (μ, radius, crash radius per `decision 34: How death works`, parent, parent orbit''s mean semi-major axis, Laplace sphere, Earth''s J2), `(body key)`; Earth Rotation Angle with the integer part of D_U kept apart; the Moon''s IAU WGCCRE 2015 leading-term rotation (no periodic terms); `body-fixed-matrix`, `latitude-longitude`, `body-texture-uv` ("Frames").
- Tests ("Frame transforms"): θ at J2000.0 and its rate within 1e-12 rev; texture (u, v) of body-fixed x and the north pole; longitude 90.246° W after 6 UT1 hours within 1e-9°; Laplace spheres within 1 % of ~9.25×10^8 m and ~6.6×10^7 m. The Moon''s synchronous rotation test is piece 4''s.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes.', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:13:44Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (95, 13, 'bodies.lisp part two: ephemerides and the Hermite cache', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/bodies.lisp, tests/bodies.lisp, docs/architecture.md, docs/design.md. μ and radii checked against gm_de440.tpc (Park et al. 2021) and IAU 2015: units.lisp unchanged. Cached body-state-into ~48 ns (Sun from Earth), ~31 ns (Moon). Deviations recorded in decision 89: Ephemeris test bounds and the start Sun''s RA (Moon Hermite bound 3 cm, 2.5 cm measured; Earth/EMB identity 1e-4 m; start Sun RA 280.5° ICRF, design.md fixed).', 'Piece 4 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: the ephemerides and their cache in `src/bodies.lisp`, as the plan''s section "4. `bodies.lisp`, part two" lists them (`decision 18: Ephemerides`, `decision 67: Ephemeris cache and the Moon''s series frame`). Needs piece 3 (the `body` list and rotations). Web access: for the JPL Horizons vectors and the DE440 digits.

- Files: `src/bodies.lisp`, `tests/bodies.lisp`; `src/units.lisp` if a constant differs from its source; `docs/architecture.md` "Ephemerides" (the two cached quantities, the global cache and the precession of `decision 67`, replacing "kept in a small table in the `game` object"; the measured cost of a cached `body-state-into`) and "Ephemeris spot checks" (Mars and Jupiter wait for milestone 4).
- Models: Sun at the origin; the EMB from Standish Table 1 (EMB row), Kepler by Newton to 1e-14 rad, analytic velocity, ecliptic → ICRF by ε; the Moon from Meeus ch. 47 (tables 47.A and 47.B in full, no nutation), precessed by Meeus eq. 21.5, velocity by ±60 s central difference; Earth = EMB − μ_Moon/(μ_Earth + μ_Moon) × Moon.
- Cache: nodes every 4,096 s for the EMB and the geocentric Moon, each a pure function of its index; cubic Hermite; direct-mapped, 64 slots per quantity.
- API: `body-state` → `(values r v)`, `body-state-into`, origins `:sun`, `:earth`, `:moon`; `body-state-series` bypasses the cache.
- Tests ("Ephemeris spot checks"): Horizons vectors committed as constants with their query in a comment (EMB from the Sun, target 3 centre 500@10; Moon from Earth, target 301 centre 500@399; 2026-01-01, 2040-01-01, 2049-06-01 00:00 TDB; bounds as in the plan); the Sun from Earth at the start near RA 281°, Dec −23° within 0.5°; Hermite vs series within 2 cm over 200 fixed times in 2040; node bit-identical computed first or after 100 others; the Earth/EMB/Moon identities within 1e-6 m and 1e-4 m; the Moon''s prime meridian within 10° of Earth at the three dates.
- Also: check μ of Sun, Earth, Moon digit by digit against Park et al. 2021 and the IAU radii; fix `units.lisp` and say so in the done note if one differs.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes, every Horizons query is reproducible from its comment, and the cost of a cached `body-state-into` (a few hundred ns at most) is measured and written in "Ephemerides".', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:21:10Z', 82, 1);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (96, 13, 'orbits.lisp: ellipses, Kepler, apsides, radius crossings', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/orbits.lisp, tests/orbits.lisp, luv-in-space.asd, docs/architecture.md (Rails, Kepler round trip, Files in load order), AGENTS.md. The semi-latus rectum is orbit-semi-latus (orbit-p is the struct predicate). Hyperbolic states signal a PLACEHOLDER(97) error. The part''s orbit tests take ~0.04 s.', 'Piece 5 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: write `src/orbits.lisp` and `tests/orbits.lisp` for ellipses as the plan''s section "5. `orbits.lisp`" lists them (`decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`). Needs pieces 1–4 (the lighting test needs the ephemerides).

- Files: `src/orbits.lisp`, `tests/orbits.lisp` (new); `luv-in-space.asd` (both systems, after `bodies`); `docs/architecture.md` "Rails" (names the `orbit` struct) and "Kepler round trip" (hyperbolic cases are piece 6''s); `AGENTS.md` "Layout" `src/` bullet kept true.
- Contents: the `orbit` struct; `state->orbit`, `orbit-state` (argument of latitude and true longitude where ω or Ω are conventional); elliptic Kepler by Newton from E₀ = M + e sin M (π for e > 0.8) to 1e-15 relative; a, p, n, period, apsis radii, `orbit-energy`, `orbit-next-apsis`, `orbit-radius-crossings` in closed form (nil outside [q, Q]); `orbit-j2-rates`.
- Tests ("Kepler round trip"): the plan''s list: round trips within 1e-9 for circular equatorial, the polar start orbit of `decision 38: Start orbit: polar`, i = 150°, e = 0.5, e = 0.9 at eight anomalies, and orbit → state → orbit; propagation there and back; Kepler residual below 1e-14 up to e = 0.99; start orbit period 92.6 min and 7,669 m/s; 800 × 90 km apsides; the K-17 crossing 2,603.07 s after apogee at −14.35° (within 0.01 s, 0.01°) and none for periapsis 1 m above; J2 Ω̇ ≈ −5.0°/day at 400 km 51.6° and |Ω̇| < 1e-15 rad/s at 90°; the start''s β −10° and the ship 25° from the Sun within 1°.

Done when: `scripts/test` passes; `./sly eval ''(orbit-period (state->orbit …))'' --package LUV-IN-SPACE` works on a hand-made state.', '2026-10-14T22:55:06Z', '2026-10-14T23:24:58Z', 82, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (97, 13, 'orbits.lisp: hyperbolas and orbit-points', 'work', 'open', NULL, NULL, 'Piece 6 of `plan 13: Simulation foundations: math, units, bodies, orbits`: extend `src/orbits.lisp` to e > 1 and add `orbit-points`, as the plan''s section "6. `orbits.lisp`: hyperbolas" lists them (`decision 46: Rails across spheres, hyperbolas and re-entry`, `decision 68: Orbit elements: one struct for every conic`). Needs piece 5.

